1
00:00:28,416 --> 00:00:32,497
The Tesseract has awakened.

2
00:00:33,045 --> 00:00:38,200
It is on a little world, a human world.

3
00:00:38,718 --> 00:00:42,241
They would wield its power,

4
00:00:42,430 --> 00:00:48,315
but our ally knows its
workings as they never will.

5
00:00:49,645 --> 00:00:52,867
He is ready to lead

6
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:58,568
and our force, our Chitauri, will follow.

7
00:00:59,989 --> 00:01:02,524
A world will be his.

8
00:01:02,616 --> 00:01:05,839
The universe, yours.

9
00:01:05,911 --> 00:01:11,711
And the humans,
what can they do but burn?

10
00:01:26,015 --> 00:01:27,218
All personnel,

11
00:01:27,266 --> 00:01:29,672
the evacuation order
has been confirmed.

12
00:02:01,467 --> 00:02:03,056
How bad is it?

13
00:02:03,177 --> 00:02:06,399
That's the problem, sir. We don't know.

14
00:02:10,059 --> 00:02:13,061
Dr Selvig read an energy surge
from the Tesseract four hours ago.

15
00:02:13,062 --> 00:02:15,038
NASA didn't authorise Selvig
to go to test phase.

16
00:02:15,147 --> 00:02:17,467
He wasn't testing it.
He wasn't even in the room.

17
00:02:17,566 --> 00:02:18,597
Spontaneous event.

18
00:02:18,651 --> 00:02:19,682
It just turned itself on?

19
00:02:20,069 --> 00:02:21,186
Where are the energy levels now?

20
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:23,597
Climbing. When Selvig couldn't
shut it down, we ordered evac.

21
00:02:23,697 --> 00:02:24,771
How long to get everyone out?

22
00:02:25,115 --> 00:02:26,533
Campus should be clear
in the next half-hour.

23
00:02:26,659 --> 00:02:27,991
Do better.

24
00:02:28,869 --> 00:02:30,931
Sir, evacuation may be futile.

25
00:02:31,038 --> 00:02:32,327
We should tell them
to go back to sleep?

26
00:02:32,623 --> 00:02:34,943
If we can't control
the Tesseract's energy,

27
00:02:35,042 --> 00:02:37,490
there may not be
a minimum safe distance.

28
00:02:37,503 --> 00:02:38,620
I need you to make sure

29
00:02:38,671 --> 00:02:40,432
the Phase 2 prototypes
are shipped out.

30
00:02:40,506 --> 00:02:42,654
Sir, is that really a priority right now?

31
00:02:42,758 --> 00:02:44,563
Until such time as the world ends,

32
00:02:44,593 --> 00:02:46,526
we will act as though
it intends to spin on.

33
00:02:47,596 --> 00:02:49,057
Clear out the tech below.

34
00:02:49,181 --> 00:02:51,330
Every piece of Phase 2
on a truck and gone.

35
00:02:51,433 --> 00:02:52,895
Yes, sir.

36
00:02:53,269 --> 00:02:54,471
With me.

37
00:02:57,439 --> 00:02:58,470
Talk to me, Doctor.

38
00:03:00,442 --> 00:03:01,904
Director.

39
00:03:02,027 --> 00:03:03,788
Is there anything we know for certain?

40
00:03:03,904 --> 00:03:06,224
The Tesseract is misbehaving.

41
00:03:06,323 --> 00:03:09,244
- Is that supposed to be funny?
- No, it's not funny at all.

42
00:03:09,326 --> 00:03:12,763
The Tesseract is not only
active, she's behaving.

43
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,154
I assume you pulled the plug.

44
00:03:14,290 --> 00:03:16,051
She's an energy source.

45
00:03:16,333 --> 00:03:19,460
We turn off the power,
she turns it back on.

46
00:03:19,461 --> 00:03:20,622
If she reaches peak level...

47
00:03:20,754 --> 00:03:24,320
We prepared for this, Doctor.
Harnessing energy from space.

48
00:03:24,383 --> 00:03:25,844
But we don't have the harness.

49
00:03:25,885 --> 00:03:27,002
My calculations are far from complete.

50
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:30,384
And she's throwing off
interference, radiation.

51
00:03:30,472 --> 00:03:31,976
Nothing harmful,
low levels of gamma radiation.

52
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:34,733
That can be harmful.

53
00:03:35,144 --> 00:03:36,648
Where's Agent Barton?

54
00:03:36,687 --> 00:03:38,534
The Hawk?

55
00:03:39,315 --> 00:03:41,033
Up in his nest, as usual.

56
00:03:42,818 --> 00:03:44,708
Agent Barton, report.

57
00:03:45,487 --> 00:03:46,733
I gave you this detail

58
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:48,413
so you could keep
a close eye on things.

59
00:03:48,574 --> 00:03:50,035
Well, I see better from a distance.

60
00:03:50,159 --> 00:03:51,920
Have you seen anything
that might set this thing off?

61
00:03:52,536 --> 00:03:54,813
Doctor, it's spiking again.

62
00:03:54,914 --> 00:03:56,375
No one's come or gone.

63
00:03:56,498 --> 00:03:58,217
And Selvig's clean.

64
00:03:58,334 --> 00:04:00,567
No contacts, no IMs.

65
00:04:01,128 --> 00:04:02,761
If there was any tampering,
sir, it wasn't at this end.

66
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:06,257
"At this end"?

67
00:04:06,383 --> 00:04:10,422
Yeah, the Cube is a doorway to
the other end of space, right?

68
00:04:12,056 --> 00:04:13,345
Doors open from both sides.

69
00:04:14,141 --> 00:04:15,558
Not yet.

70
00:05:23,419 --> 00:05:26,554
Sir, please put down the spear.

71
00:06:05,794 --> 00:06:06,868
You have heart.

72
00:06:37,659 --> 00:06:39,206
Please don't.

73
00:06:40,829 --> 00:06:41,947
I still need that.

74
00:06:42,331 --> 00:06:43,877
This doesn't have to get any messier.

75
00:06:43,999 --> 00:06:45,117
Of course it does.

76
00:06:45,334 --> 00:06:47,095
I've come too far for anything else.

77
00:06:49,004 --> 00:06:51,925
I am Loki, of Asgard

78
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:55,248
and I am burdened with
glorious purpose.

79
00:06:55,344 --> 00:06:56,890
Loki,

80
00:06:57,262 --> 00:06:58,680
brother of Thor.

81
00:06:58,806 --> 00:07:01,039
We have no quarrel with your people.

82
00:07:01,475 --> 00:07:04,224
An ant has no quarrel with a boot.

83
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:06,567
Are you planning to step on us?

84
00:07:07,022 --> 00:07:10,202
I come with glad tidings

85
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:13,078
of a world made free.

86
00:07:13,529 --> 00:07:14,646
Free from what?

87
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:15,983
Freedom.

88
00:07:16,698 --> 00:07:19,147
Freedom is life's great lie.

89
00:07:19,535 --> 00:07:22,886
Once you accept that, in your heart,

90
00:07:27,376 --> 00:07:29,137
you will know peace.

91
00:07:29,628 --> 00:07:32,206
Yeah, you say "peace,"

92
00:07:32,297 --> 00:07:34,274
I kind of think you mean the other thing.

93
00:07:34,383 --> 00:07:36,960
Sir, Director Fury is stalling.

94
00:07:37,052 --> 00:07:38,513
This place is about to blow

95
00:07:38,554 --> 00:07:40,015
and drop a hundred feet of rock on us.

96
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:42,757
He means to bury us.

97
00:07:42,891 --> 00:07:44,094
Like the pharaohs of old.

98
00:07:44,268 --> 00:07:46,372
He's right. The portal
is collapsing in on itself.

99
00:07:46,478 --> 00:07:48,627
We've got maybe two minutes
before this goes critical.

100
00:07:48,897 --> 00:07:49,928
Well, then.

101
00:08:05,664 --> 00:08:06,781
I need these vehicles.

102
00:08:10,878 --> 00:08:12,982
- Who's that?
- They didn't tell me.

103
00:08:16,216 --> 00:08:17,548
Hill!

104
00:08:17,759 --> 00:08:18,760
Do you CODY?

105
00:08:20,095 --> 00:08:21,169
Barton has turned.

106
00:08:34,109 --> 00:08:37,030
They have the Tesseract!
Shut them down!

107
00:09:13,649 --> 00:09:15,753
Okay, let's go. No, leave it. Go!

108
00:09:32,334 --> 00:09:34,267
We're clear upstairs, sir.
You need to go.

109
00:11:06,303 --> 00:11:07,720
Director?

110
00:11:08,096 --> 00:11:09,471
Director Fury, do you copy?

111
00:11:09,765 --> 00:11:12,170
The Tesseract is with a hostile force.

112
00:11:12,267 --> 00:11:14,501
I have men down. Hill?

113
00:11:15,103 --> 00:11:17,080
A lot of men still under.

114
00:11:17,189 --> 00:11:18,993
I don't know how many survivors.

115
00:11:19,107 --> 00:11:20,353
Sound a general call.

116
00:11:20,484 --> 00:11:22,073
I want every living soul
not working rescue

117
00:11:22,110 --> 00:11:23,141
looking for that briefcase.

118
00:11:23,195 --> 00:11:24,312
Roger that.

119
00:11:24,446 --> 00:11:27,925
Coulson, get back to base.
This is a Level Seven.

120
00:11:29,117 --> 00:11:30,750
As of right now,

121
00:11:30,827 --> 00:11:32,202
we are at war.

122
00:11:34,122 --> 00:11:35,497
What do we do?

123
00:12:12,285 --> 00:12:15,871
This is not how I wanted this evening to go.

124
00:12:15,872 --> 00:12:17,720
I know how you wanted this evening to go.

125
00:12:17,749 --> 00:12:18,909
Believe me

126
00:12:18,959 --> 00:12:20,032
this is better.

127
00:12:21,169 --> 00:12:22,930
Who are you working for?

128
00:12:23,422 --> 00:12:24,883
Lermentov, yes?

129
00:12:26,967 --> 00:12:28,513
Does he think

130
00:12:28,677 --> 00:12:30,395
we have to go through him

131
00:12:30,846 --> 00:12:32,392
to move our cargo?

132
00:12:33,849 --> 00:12:38,531
I thought General Solohob
is in charge of the export business.

133
00:12:38,770 --> 00:12:40,832
Solohob

134
00:12:40,897 --> 00:12:43,088
a bagman, a front.

135
00:12:45,402 --> 00:12:49,784
Your outdated information betrays you.

136
00:12:51,199 --> 00:12:53,906
The famous Black Widow

137
00:12:55,579 --> 00:12:59,961
and she turns out to be
simply another pretty face.

138
00:13:00,834 --> 00:13:03,970
You really think I'm pretty?

139
00:13:06,548 --> 00:13:08,911
Tell Lermentov we don't need him

140
00:13:09,092 --> 00:13:12,830
to move the tanks.

141
00:13:13,638 --> 00:13:16,388
Tell him he is out.

142
00:13:16,683 --> 00:13:18,401
Well...

143
00:13:21,188 --> 00:13:22,863
...you may have to write it down.

144
00:13:31,907 --> 00:13:33,453
It's for her.

145
00:13:36,828 --> 00:13:38,203
You listen carefully

146
00:13:38,246 --> 00:13:40,609
You're at 1-14 Silensky Plaza, 3rd floor.

147
00:13:41,082 --> 00:13:43,102
We have an F-22
exactly eight miles out.

148
00:13:44,002 --> 00:13:46,064
Put the woman on the phone
or I will blow up the block

149
00:13:46,087 --> 00:13:48,236
before you can make the lobby.

150
00:13:54,763 --> 00:13:56,997
- We need you to come in.
- Are you kidding? I'm working.

151
00:13:57,098 --> 00:13:58,301
This takes precedence.

152
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,318
I'm in the middle of an interrogation.

153
00:14:00,393 --> 00:14:02,069
This moron is giving me everything.

154
00:14:02,604 --> 00:14:05,139
I don't give everything.

155
00:14:06,650 --> 00:14:07,939
Look, you can't pull me
out of this right now.

156
00:14:07,984 --> 00:14:09,015
Natasha...

157
00:14:10,737 --> 00:14:12,112
Barton's been compromised.

158
00:14:15,450 --> 00:14:17,383
Let me put you on hold.

159
00:14:59,035 --> 00:15:00,066
Where is Barton now?

160
00:15:00,203 --> 00:15:01,535
- We don't know.
- But he's alive?

161
00:15:01,913 --> 00:15:04,620
We think so. I'll brief you on
everything when you get back.

162
00:15:04,916 --> 00:15:07,065
But first, we need you to
talk to the big guy.

163
00:15:07,502 --> 00:15:10,423
Coulson, you know that Stark trusts me
about as far as he can throw me.

164
00:15:10,505 --> 00:15:13,770
I've got Stark. You get the big guy.

165
00:15:38,700 --> 00:15:39,731
Who are you?

166
00:15:40,201 --> 00:15:41,362
Get out!

167
00:15:41,411 --> 00:15:44,031
There is sickness here!

168
00:15:44,039 --> 00:15:45,070
You're a doctor.

169
00:15:46,750 --> 00:15:48,124
My father's not waking up!

170
00:15:48,168 --> 00:15:49,843
He has a fever and he's moaning

171
00:15:49,878 --> 00:15:51,081
but his eyes won't open.

172
00:15:51,129 --> 00:15:52,160
Slow down.

173
00:15:53,548 --> 00:15:54,708
My father...

174
00:15:57,344 --> 00:15:58,375
Like them?

175
00:16:02,349 --> 00:16:03,681
Please.

176
00:16:30,794 --> 00:16:33,199
You should've got paid
up front, Banner.

177
00:16:33,296 --> 00:16:34,671
You know, for a man

178
00:16:34,714 --> 00:16:36,046
who's supposed to be avoiding stress

179
00:16:36,216 --> 00:16:39,351
you picked a hell of a place to settle.

180
00:16:41,221 --> 00:16:43,412
Avoiding stress isn't the secret.

181
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,831
Then what is it? Yoga?

182
00:16:47,310 --> 00:16:50,618
You brought me to the edge of
the city. Smart.

183
00:16:51,064 --> 00:16:55,274
I assume the whole place
is surrounded.

184
00:16:55,568 --> 00:16:57,029
Just you and me.

185
00:16:58,196 --> 00:17:00,344
And your actress buddy?

186
00:17:00,448 --> 00:17:02,253
Is she a spy, too?
They start that young?

187
00:17:02,826 --> 00:17:04,158
I did.

188
00:17:04,285 --> 00:17:05,403
Who are you?

189
00:17:05,453 --> 00:17:06,484
Natasha Romanoff.

190
00:17:09,999 --> 00:17:11,417
Are you here to kill me, Ms Romanoff?

191
00:17:11,543 --> 00:17:14,207
Because that's not going to
work out for everyone.

192
00:17:14,462 --> 00:17:16,696
No, of course not. I'm here
on behalf of S.H.I.E.L.D.

193
00:17:18,675 --> 00:17:20,092
S.H.I.E.L.D.

194
00:17:21,970 --> 00:17:23,001
How did they find me?

195
00:17:23,138 --> 00:17:24,599
We never lost you, Doctor.

196
00:17:24,806 --> 00:17:26,138
We've kept our distance.

197
00:17:26,182 --> 00:17:27,943
Even helped keep some other
interested parties

198
00:17:27,976 --> 00:17:29,136
off your scent.

199
00:17:29,686 --> 00:17:30,760
Why?

200
00:17:30,812 --> 00:17:33,304
Nick Fury seems to trust you.

201
00:17:33,398 --> 00:17:34,773
But now we need you to come in.

202
00:17:35,984 --> 00:17:37,659
What if I say no?

203
00:17:38,069 --> 00:17:40,088
I'll persuade you.

204
00:17:42,323 --> 00:17:46,834
And what if the other guy says no?

205
00:17:47,370 --> 00:17:49,088
You've been more than a year
without an incident.

206
00:17:49,205 --> 00:17:51,568
I don't think you want to
break that streak.

207
00:17:54,002 --> 00:17:56,751
Well, I don't every time get what I want.

208
00:17:57,672 --> 00:17:59,691
Doctor, we're facing a potential
global catastrophe.

209
00:18:00,717 --> 00:18:03,681
Well, those I actively try to avoid.

210
00:18:04,179 --> 00:18:06,327
This

211
00:18:06,431 --> 00:18:08,622
is the Tesseract.

212
00:18:08,683 --> 00:18:11,604
It has the potential energy
to wipe out the planet.

213
00:18:14,647 --> 00:18:16,580
What does Fury want me to do,
swallow it?

214
00:18:17,025 --> 00:18:19,345
He wants you to find it. It's been taken.

215
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:24,658
It emits a gamma signature
that's too weak for us to trace.

216
00:18:24,699 --> 00:18:27,749
There's no one that knows
gamma radiation like you do.

217
00:18:27,827 --> 00:18:30,405
If there was, that's where I'd be.

218
00:18:31,206 --> 00:18:33,225
So, Fury isn't after the monster?

219
00:18:33,583 --> 00:18:34,915
Not that he's told me.

220
00:18:35,043 --> 00:18:37,319
And he tells you everything?

221
00:18:37,879 --> 00:18:39,555
Talk to Fury. He needs you on this.

222
00:18:39,589 --> 00:18:40,792
He needs me in a cage?

223
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:41,841
No one's going to put you in a...

224
00:18:41,883 --> 00:18:42,884
Stop lying to me!

225
00:18:46,930 --> 00:18:49,679
I'm sorry. That was mean.

226
00:18:50,517 --> 00:18:52,793
I just wanted to see what you'd do.

227
00:18:53,895 --> 00:18:56,988
Why don't we do this the easy way

228
00:18:57,065 --> 00:18:58,397
where you don't use that

229
00:18:58,525 --> 00:19:02,348
and the other guy
doesn't make a mess.

230
00:19:03,238 --> 00:19:04,612
Okay?

231
00:19:05,532 --> 00:19:06,949
Natasha?

232
00:19:12,539 --> 00:19:13,656
Stand down.

233
00:19:14,541 --> 00:19:16,173
We're good here.

234
00:19:17,919 --> 00:19:19,294
"Just you and me."

235
00:19:21,631 --> 00:19:24,338
This is out of line, Director.

236
00:19:24,425 --> 00:19:26,960
You're dealing
with forces you can't control.

237
00:19:27,262 --> 00:19:30,870
You ever been in a war,
Councilman? In a firefight?

238
00:19:30,932 --> 00:19:33,853
Did you feel
an overabundance of control?

239
00:19:33,935 --> 00:19:37,437
You're saying that this Asgard
is declaring war on our planet?

240
00:19:37,438 --> 00:19:40,188
Not Asgard. Loki.

241
00:19:40,275 --> 00:19:43,193
He can't be working alone.
What about the other one?

242
00:19:43,194 --> 00:19:44,312
His brother.

243
00:19:44,362 --> 00:19:46,381
Our intelligence says
Thor is not a hostile

244
00:19:46,614 --> 00:19:47,645
but he's worlds away.

245
00:19:47,782 --> 00:19:49,672
We can't depend on him to help, either.

246
00:19:49,701 --> 00:19:50,732
It's up to us.

247
00:19:50,785 --> 00:19:53,534
Which is why you
should be focusing on Phase 2.

248
00:19:53,621 --> 00:19:54,824
It was designed for exactly this...

249
00:19:55,123 --> 00:19:58,044
Phase 2 isn't ready. Our enemy is.

250
00:19:58,543 --> 00:20:00,176
We need a response team.

251
00:20:00,295 --> 00:20:02,528
The Avengers Initiative was shut down.

252
00:20:02,630 --> 00:20:04,520
This isn't about the Avengers.

253
00:20:04,799 --> 00:20:06,002
We've seen the list.

254
00:20:06,134 --> 00:20:08,454
You're running the world's greatest
covert security network

255
00:20:08,469 --> 00:20:10,188
and you're going to leave
the fate of the human race

256
00:20:10,263 --> 00:20:11,595
to a handful of freaks.

257
00:20:11,639 --> 00:20:13,659
I'm not leaving anything to anyone.

258
00:20:13,766 --> 00:20:15,743
We need a response team.

259
00:20:16,227 --> 00:20:19,063
These people may be isolated,
unbalanced even

260
00:20:19,147 --> 00:20:23,357
but I believe with the right push
they can be exactly what we need.

261
00:20:23,610 --> 00:20:25,027
You believe?

262
00:20:25,153 --> 00:20:28,589
War isn't won by sentiment, Director.

263
00:20:29,407 --> 00:20:32,930
No, it's won by soldiers.

264
00:20:52,388 --> 00:20:53,849
There's not enough time.

265
00:20:54,140 --> 00:20:55,729
I got to put her in the water!

266
00:21:00,939 --> 00:21:02,056
You won't be alone.

267
00:21:02,690 --> 00:21:04,065
Oh, my God.

268
00:21:04,651 --> 00:21:05,896
This guy is still alive!

269
00:21:30,843 --> 00:21:32,691
Trouble sleeping?

270
00:21:33,930 --> 00:21:36,465
I slept for 70 years, sir.
I think I've had my fill.

271
00:21:38,142 --> 00:21:41,923
Then you should be out,
celebrating, seeing the world.

272
00:21:47,902 --> 00:21:50,866
When I went under,
the world was at war.

273
00:21:50,947 --> 00:21:52,536
I wake up, they say we won.

274
00:21:53,491 --> 00:21:54,780
They didn't say what we lost.

275
00:21:55,618 --> 00:21:57,767
We've made some mistakes
along the way.

276
00:21:58,371 --> 00:21:59,788
Some, very recently.

277
00:22:01,582 --> 00:22:02,872
Are you here with a mission, sir?

278
00:22:02,917 --> 00:22:03,991
I am.

279
00:22:04,043 --> 00:22:05,504
Trying to get me back in the world?

280
00:22:06,212 --> 00:22:07,673
Trying to save it.

281
00:22:12,552 --> 00:22:14,656
HYDRA'S secret weapon.

282
00:22:14,762 --> 00:22:16,610
Howard Stark fished that
out of the ocean

283
00:22:16,639 --> 00:22:17,842
when he was looking for you.

284
00:22:18,641 --> 00:22:20,016
He thought what we think.

285
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:24,512
The Tesseract could be the key
to unlimited sustainable energy.

286
00:22:25,148 --> 00:22:28,843
That's something
the world sorely needs.

287
00:22:30,486 --> 00:22:31,732
Who took it from you?

288
00:22:31,863 --> 00:22:33,366
He's called Loki.

289
00:22:33,489 --> 00:22:35,852
He's not from around here.

290
00:22:36,617 --> 00:22:38,766
There's a lot we'll have to
bring you up to speed on

291
00:22:38,786 --> 00:22:40,076
if you're in.

292
00:22:40,955 --> 00:22:42,716
The world has gotten even stranger

293
00:22:42,790 --> 00:22:43,950
than you already know.

294
00:22:44,667 --> 00:22:47,073
At this point, I doubt
anything would surprise me.

295
00:22:47,879 --> 00:22:49,340
Ten bucks says you're wrong.

296
00:22:51,299 --> 00:22:52,760
There's a debriefing packet

297
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:55,292
waiting for you back at your apartment.

298
00:22:57,388 --> 00:22:59,407
Is there anything you can
tell us about the Tesseract

299
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:00,886
that we ought to know now?

300
00:23:01,142 --> 00:23:03,548
You should have left it in the ocean.

301
00:23:36,177 --> 00:23:39,141
Good to go on this end.
The rest is up to you.

302
00:23:39,222 --> 00:23:40,639
You disconnected
the transmission lines?

303
00:23:40,681 --> 00:23:41,799
Are we off the grid?

304
00:23:41,849 --> 00:23:44,083
Stark Tower is about to become
a beacon

305
00:23:44,143 --> 00:23:45,518
of self-sustaining clean energy.

306
00:23:45,728 --> 00:23:47,877
Well, assuming
the arc reactor takes over

307
00:23:47,897 --> 00:23:49,229
and it actually works.

308
00:23:49,482 --> 00:23:50,857
I assume.

309
00:23:51,025 --> 00:23:52,056
Light her up.

310
00:23:57,865 --> 00:23:58,896
How does it look?

311
00:23:59,033 --> 00:24:01,782
Like Christmas, but with more me.

312
00:24:01,869 --> 00:24:03,545
We've got to go wider on
the public awareness campaign.

313
00:24:03,579 --> 00:24:04,697
You need to do some press.

314
00:24:05,248 --> 00:24:06,365
I'm in DC tomorrow,

315
00:24:06,415 --> 00:24:07,962
I'm working on the zoning
for the next three buildings.

316
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,277
Pepper, you're killing me.
The moment, remember?

317
00:24:10,753 --> 00:24:11,913
Enjoy the moment.

318
00:24:11,963 --> 00:24:12,994
Get in here and I will.

319
00:24:16,551 --> 00:24:19,558
Sir, Agent Coulson of
S.H.I.E.L.D. is on the line.

320
00:24:20,012 --> 00:24:21,086
I'm not in.

321
00:24:21,681 --> 00:24:23,098
I'm actually out.

322
00:24:30,189 --> 00:24:32,981
Sir, I'm afraid he's insisting.

323
00:24:33,067 --> 00:24:35,602
Grow a spine, Jarvis. I got a date.

324
00:24:40,324 --> 00:24:43,417
Levels are holding steady, I think.

325
00:24:43,494 --> 00:24:45,771
Of course they are.
I was directly involved.

326
00:24:45,872 --> 00:24:47,117
Which brings me to my next question.

327
00:24:47,206 --> 00:24:49,311
How does it feel to be a genius?

328
00:24:49,417 --> 00:24:51,737
Well, I really wouldn't know,
now would I?

329
00:24:51,836 --> 00:24:56,518
What do you mean?
All this came from you.

330
00:24:56,549 --> 00:25:00,028
No, all this came from that.

331
00:25:00,386 --> 00:25:02,577
Give yourself some credit. Please.

332
00:25:02,889 --> 00:25:04,779
Stark Tower is your baby.

333
00:25:04,891 --> 00:25:07,082
Give yourself 12% of the credit.

334
00:25:07,518 --> 00:25:08,678
12%?

335
00:25:08,769 --> 00:25:10,015
An argument can be made for 15.

336
00:25:10,271 --> 00:25:11,904
12%? My baby?

337
00:25:12,023 --> 00:25:13,741
Well, I did do all the heavy lifting.

338
00:25:13,774 --> 00:25:15,321
Literally, I lifted the heavy things.

339
00:25:15,860 --> 00:25:18,266
And, sorry, but the security snafu?

340
00:25:18,279 --> 00:25:19,825
That was on you.

341
00:25:19,864 --> 00:25:21,883
- My private elevator...
- You mean our elevator?

342
00:25:22,158 --> 00:25:24,950
...It was teeming with sweaty workmen.

343
00:25:25,036 --> 00:25:27,528
I'm going to pay for that
comment about percentages

344
00:25:27,622 --> 00:25:29,297
in some subtle way later, aren't I?

345
00:25:29,999 --> 00:25:31,331
It's not going to be that subtle.

346
00:25:31,459 --> 00:25:32,791
I'll tell you what.

347
00:25:32,919 --> 00:25:35,282
The next building is gonna
say "Potts" on the tower.

348
00:25:35,463 --> 00:25:36,795
On the lease.

349
00:25:37,882 --> 00:25:40,116
Call your mom. Can you bunk over?

350
00:25:40,218 --> 00:25:41,549
Sir, the telephone.

351
00:25:41,677 --> 00:25:44,212
I'm afraid my protocols
are being overridden.

352
00:25:44,305 --> 00:25:46,066
Mr Stark, we need to talk.

353
00:25:46,307 --> 00:25:48,755
You have reached the life
model decoy of Tony Stark.

354
00:25:49,101 --> 00:25:51,034
- Please leave a message.
- This is urgent.

355
00:25:51,312 --> 00:25:53,159
Then leave it urgently.

356
00:25:54,649 --> 00:25:55,851
Security breach. It's on you.

357
00:25:55,983 --> 00:25:58,690
- Mr Stark.
- Phil! Come in.

358
00:25:58,694 --> 00:25:59,725
"Phil"?

359
00:25:59,820 --> 00:26:00,894
I can't stay.

360
00:26:01,197 --> 00:26:02,486
His first name is "Agent."

361
00:26:02,907 --> 00:26:04,239
Come on in. We're celebrating.

362
00:26:04,283 --> 00:26:06,173
Which is why he can't stay.

363
00:26:06,494 --> 00:26:08,556
We need you to look this over
as soon as possible.

364
00:26:08,663 --> 00:26:09,736
I don't like being handed things.

365
00:26:09,872 --> 00:26:11,204
That's fine, because
I love to be handed things.

366
00:26:11,332 --> 00:26:12,749
So, let's trade.

367
00:26:14,252 --> 00:26:15,841
Thank you.

368
00:26:16,963 --> 00:26:19,111
Official consulting hours
are between 8 and 5

369
00:26:19,131 --> 00:26:20,162
every other Thursday.

370
00:26:20,508 --> 00:26:21,539
This isn't a consultation.

371
00:26:21,592 --> 00:26:22,710
Is this about the Avengers?

372
00:26:23,261 --> 00:26:25,237
Which I know nothing about.

373
00:26:25,346 --> 00:26:27,966
The Avengers Initiative
was scrapped, I thought.

374
00:26:28,057 --> 00:26:29,346
And I didn't even qualify.

375
00:26:29,392 --> 00:26:30,423
I didn't know that either.

376
00:26:30,810 --> 00:26:33,812
Apparently I'm volatile, self-obsessed,

377
00:26:33,813 --> 00:26:34,973
don't play well with others.

378
00:26:35,356 --> 00:26:36,430
That I did know.

379
00:26:36,482 --> 00:26:38,243
This isn't about personality
profiles any more.

380
00:26:38,276 --> 00:26:40,768
Whatever. Ms Potts, got a second?

381
00:26:40,861 --> 00:26:41,892
Half a mo.

382
00:26:47,118 --> 00:26:49,352
You know, I thought we were
having a moment.

383
00:26:49,704 --> 00:26:51,036
I was having 12% of a moment.

384
00:26:52,456 --> 00:26:55,034
This seems serious.
Phil's pretty shaken.

385
00:26:55,126 --> 00:26:57,188
How would you know if it's...
Why is he "Phil"?

386
00:26:57,295 --> 00:26:59,142
What is all this?

387
00:26:59,255 --> 00:27:00,930
This is

388
00:27:01,507 --> 00:27:02,538
this.

389
00:27:09,849 --> 00:27:11,009
I'm going to take the jet to DC tonight.

390
00:27:11,058 --> 00:27:12,218
Tomorrow.

391
00:27:12,393 --> 00:27:14,799
You have homework.
You have a lot of homework.

392
00:27:15,062 --> 00:27:16,823
Well, What if I didn't?

393
00:27:17,398 --> 00:27:18,815
- If you didn't?
- Yeah.

394
00:27:18,941 --> 00:27:21,218
You mean when you've finished?

395
00:27:22,236 --> 00:27:25,630
Well, then...

396
00:27:30,453 --> 00:27:31,785
Square deal. Fly safe.

397
00:27:36,208 --> 00:27:37,411
Work hard.

398
00:27:40,212 --> 00:27:42,060
So, any chance
you're driving by LaGuardia?

399
00:27:42,173 --> 00:27:45,051
- I can drop you.
- Fantastic.

400
00:27:45,051 --> 00:27:46,124
I want to hear

401
00:27:46,177 --> 00:27:47,981
about the cellist. Is that still a thing?

402
00:27:48,054 --> 00:27:49,299
She moved back to Portland.

403
00:27:49,430 --> 00:27:52,222
What? Boo!

404
00:28:00,566 --> 00:28:03,101
We're about 40 minutes
out from home base, sir.

405
00:28:06,697 --> 00:28:10,520
So, this Dr Banner was trying
to replicate the serum they used on me?

406
00:28:10,576 --> 00:28:12,209
A lot of people were.

407
00:28:12,328 --> 00:28:13,832
You were the world's first superhero.

408
00:28:14,663 --> 00:28:17,540
Banner thought gamma radiation
might hold the key to unlocking

409
00:28:17,541 --> 00:28:18,831
Erskine's original formula.

410
00:28:19,627 --> 00:28:21,131
Didn't really go his way, did it?

411
00:28:21,712 --> 00:28:23,259
Not so much.

412
00:28:23,381 --> 00:28:26,044
When he's not that thing, though,
the guy's like a Stephen Hawking.

413
00:28:28,302 --> 00:28:30,536
He's like a smart person.

414
00:28:32,681 --> 00:28:33,927
I gotta say,

415
00:28:34,016 --> 00:28:36,551
it's an honor to meet you officially.

416
00:28:37,561 --> 00:28:39,194
I've sort of met you. I mean,

417
00:28:39,230 --> 00:28:40,863
I watched you while you were sleeping.

418
00:28:42,858 --> 00:28:45,221
I mean, I was present

419
00:28:45,277 --> 00:28:48,757
while you were
unconscious from the ice.

420
00:28:48,781 --> 00:28:51,187
You know, it's really just a huge honor

421
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:53,005
to have you on board this...

422
00:28:53,536 --> 00:28:55,512
I hope I'm the man for the job.

423
00:28:55,621 --> 00:28:58,629
Oh, you are. Absolutely.

424
00:28:58,707 --> 00:29:01,758
We made some modifications
to the uniform.

425
00:29:01,836 --> 00:29:03,382
I had a little design input.

426
00:29:03,504 --> 00:29:04,793
The uniform?

427
00:29:05,005 --> 00:29:07,583
Aren't the stars and stripes a little

428
00:29:08,426 --> 00:29:09,887
old-fashioned?

429
00:29:10,803 --> 00:29:12,822
With everything that's happening

430
00:29:12,847 --> 00:29:14,565
and the things that are about
to come to light,

431
00:29:15,474 --> 00:29:19,083
people might just need
a little old-fashioned.

432
00:29:51,719 --> 00:29:54,812
The Chitauri grow restless.

433
00:29:54,889 --> 00:29:56,693
Let them gird themselves.

434
00:29:56,724 --> 00:29:58,442
I will lead them in the glorious battle.

435
00:29:58,476 --> 00:29:59,593
Battle?

436
00:30:00,686 --> 00:30:03,908
Against the meagre might of Earth?

437
00:30:03,981 --> 00:30:06,945
Glorious, not lengthy.

438
00:30:07,026 --> 00:30:11,021
If your force
is as formidable as you claim.

439
00:30:11,071 --> 00:30:13,392
You question us?

440
00:30:13,741 --> 00:30:15,975
You question him,

441
00:30:16,035 --> 00:30:18,612
he who put the sceptre in your hand?

442
00:30:18,704 --> 00:30:21,496
Who gave you ancient knowledge
and new purpose

443
00:30:21,665 --> 00:30:24,918
when you were cast out, defeated?

444
00:30:24,919 --> 00:30:26,895
I was a king!

445
00:30:27,004 --> 00:30:29,324
The rightful king of Asgard,

446
00:30:29,381 --> 00:30:30,455
betrayed.

447
00:30:31,383 --> 00:30:34,004
Your ambition is little

448
00:30:34,011 --> 00:30:36,847
and born of childish need.

449
00:30:37,181 --> 00:30:39,286
We look beyond the Earth

450
00:30:39,391 --> 00:30:42,227
to the greater worlds
the Tesseract will unveil.

451
00:30:42,603 --> 00:30:44,149
You don't have the Tesseract yet.

452
00:30:46,815 --> 00:30:47,846
I don't threaten.

453
00:30:49,610 --> 00:30:52,274
But until I open the doors,

454
00:30:52,363 --> 00:30:56,143
until your force is mine to command,

455
00:30:56,742 --> 00:30:58,632
you are but words.

456
00:30:58,744 --> 00:31:02,868
You will have your war, Asgardian.

457
00:31:04,500 --> 00:31:06,605
If you fail,

458
00:31:07,503 --> 00:31:12,100
if the Tesseract is kept from us,

459
00:31:12,132 --> 00:31:16,643
there will be no realm, no barren moon,

460
00:31:16,679 --> 00:31:20,115
no crevice where he cannot find you.

461
00:31:21,559 --> 00:31:24,437
You think you know pain?

462
00:31:24,520 --> 00:31:30,105
He will make you long
for something sweet as pain.

463
00:31:59,388 --> 00:32:00,505
Stow the captain's gear.

464
00:32:00,556 --> 00:32:01,630
Yes, sir.

465
00:32:03,100 --> 00:32:06,365
Agent Romanoff, Captain Rogers.

466
00:32:06,437 --> 00:32:07,811
- Ma'am.
- Hi.

467
00:32:07,938 --> 00:32:08,969
They need you on the bridge.

468
00:32:09,023 --> 00:32:10,612
They're starting the face-trace.

469
00:32:10,733 --> 00:32:11,893
See you there.

470
00:32:13,569 --> 00:32:17,564
It was quite the buzz around here,
finding you in the ice.

471
00:32:17,990 --> 00:32:20,697
I thought Coulson was gonna swoon.

472
00:32:20,784 --> 00:32:23,792
Did he ask you to sign
his Captain America trading cards yet?

473
00:32:23,871 --> 00:32:25,160
Trading cards?

474
00:32:25,289 --> 00:32:27,351
They're vintage. He's very proud.

475
00:32:29,209 --> 00:32:30,584
Dr Banner.

476
00:32:32,212 --> 00:32:33,587
Yeah, hi.

477
00:32:34,048 --> 00:32:35,337
They told me you would be coming.

478
00:32:35,382 --> 00:32:36,757
Word is, you can find the Cube.

479
00:32:38,093 --> 00:32:39,726
Is that the only word on me?

480
00:32:40,054 --> 00:32:41,299
Only word I care about.

481
00:32:44,141 --> 00:32:46,547
It must be strange for you, all of this.

482
00:32:47,269 --> 00:32:50,061
Well, this is actually kind of familiar.

483
00:32:50,064 --> 00:32:52,813
Gentlemen, you might want
to step inside in a minute.

484
00:32:53,108 --> 00:32:55,987
It's going to get a little hard to breathe.

485
00:32:56,862 --> 00:32:58,451
Flight crew, secure the deck.

486
00:33:03,160 --> 00:33:04,836
Is this a submarine?

487
00:33:05,329 --> 00:33:06,360
Really?

488
00:33:06,413 --> 00:33:10,365
They want me in a submerged,
pressurised, metal container?

489
00:33:36,276 --> 00:33:38,725
No, no, this is much worse.

490
00:34:08,809 --> 00:34:11,601
Hover power check complete.
Position cyclic.

491
00:34:11,687 --> 00:34:13,878
Increase collective to 8.0%.

492
00:34:19,194 --> 00:34:21,600
Preparing for maximum
performance takeoff.

493
00:34:21,655 --> 00:34:23,202
Increase output to capacity.

494
00:34:23,282 --> 00:34:25,516
Power plant performing at capacity.

495
00:34:25,617 --> 00:34:27,207
We are clear.

496
00:34:27,327 --> 00:34:28,874
All engines operating.

497
00:34:28,996 --> 00:34:33,807
S.H.I.E.L.D. Emergency
Protocol 193.6 in effect.

498
00:34:33,876 --> 00:34:36,582
- We are at level, sir.
- Good.

499
00:34:36,837 --> 00:34:37,868
Let's vanish.

500
00:34:38,005 --> 00:34:40,239
Engage retro-reflection panels.

501
00:34:56,023 --> 00:34:57,268
Reflection panels engaged.

502
00:34:57,983 --> 00:34:59,444
Gentlemen.

503
00:35:11,371 --> 00:35:12,574
Doctor, thank you for coming.

504
00:35:14,875 --> 00:35:16,808
Thanks for asking nicely.

505
00:35:16,919 --> 00:35:19,453
So, how long am I staying?

506
00:35:19,755 --> 00:35:21,388
Once we get our hands on
the Tesseract,

507
00:35:21,423 --> 00:35:22,712
you're in the wind.

508
00:35:22,758 --> 00:35:24,691
Where are you with that?

509
00:35:24,718 --> 00:35:26,608
We're sweeping every
wirelessly accessible

510
00:35:26,637 --> 00:35:27,668
camera on the planet.

511
00:35:28,347 --> 00:35:30,280
Cell phones, laptops...

512
00:35:30,891 --> 00:35:34,143
If it's connected to a satellite,
it's eyes and ears for us.

513
00:35:34,144 --> 00:35:35,476
That's still not gonna find them in time.

514
00:35:35,521 --> 00:35:36,638
You have to narrow your field.

515
00:35:36,730 --> 00:35:38,835
How many spectrometers
do you have access to?

516
00:35:39,233 --> 00:35:40,951
- How many are there?
- Call every lab you know.

517
00:35:41,068 --> 00:35:42,873
Tell them to put
the spectrometers on the roof

518
00:35:42,903 --> 00:35:44,278
and calibrate them for gamma rays.

519
00:35:44,530 --> 00:35:47,623
I'll rough out a tracking algorithm,
basic cluster recognition.

520
00:35:47,825 --> 00:35:50,359
At least we could rule out a few places.

521
00:35:50,702 --> 00:35:52,635
Do you have somewhere
for me to work?

522
00:35:52,913 --> 00:35:53,987
Agent Romanoff,

523
00:35:54,039 --> 00:35:56,230
could you show Dr Banner
to his laboratory, please?

524
00:35:57,334 --> 00:35:59,568
You're gonna love it, Doc.
We got all the toys.

525
00:36:00,254 --> 00:36:02,144
Put it over there.

526
00:36:04,007 --> 00:36:06,241
Where did you find all these people?

527
00:36:06,343 --> 00:36:09,264
S.H.I.E.L.D. has no shortage
of enemies, Doctor.

528
00:36:09,763 --> 00:36:10,966
Is this the stuff you need?

529
00:36:11,098 --> 00:36:12,129
Yeah, iridium.

530
00:36:12,182 --> 00:36:14,932
It's found in meteorites.
It forms anti-protons.

531
00:36:15,018 --> 00:36:16,737
It's very hard to get hold of.

532
00:36:16,854 --> 00:36:18,615
Especially if S.H.I.E.L.D.
knows you need it.

533
00:36:18,647 --> 00:36:20,108
Well, I didn't know.

534
00:36:20,190 --> 00:36:21,479
Hey!

535
00:36:21,608 --> 00:36:23,799
The Tesseract has shown me so much.

536
00:36:24,361 --> 00:36:26,251
It's more than knowledge. It's truth.

537
00:36:26,280 --> 00:36:27,311
I know.

538
00:36:28,073 --> 00:36:29,963
What did it show you, Agent Barton?

539
00:36:31,118 --> 00:36:32,492
My next target.

540
00:36:32,536 --> 00:36:33,567
Tell me what you need.

541
00:36:37,207 --> 00:36:39,140
I need a distraction.

542
00:36:39,835 --> 00:36:41,339
And an eyeball.

543
00:36:47,885 --> 00:36:50,634
I mean, if it's not too much trouble.

544
00:36:50,637 --> 00:36:51,755
No, no. It's fine.

545
00:36:54,975 --> 00:36:56,693
It's a vintage set.

546
00:36:56,810 --> 00:36:59,173
It took me a couple of years
to collect them all.

547
00:37:01,648 --> 00:37:02,766
Near mint.

548
00:37:02,900 --> 00:37:04,361
Slight foxing around the edges, but...

549
00:37:04,484 --> 00:37:06,977
We got a hit. A 67% match.

550
00:37:07,279 --> 00:37:08,997
Wait. Cross match, 79%.

551
00:37:10,324 --> 00:37:11,355
Location?

552
00:37:11,658 --> 00:37:14,579
Stuttgart, Germany. 28 Königstrasse.

553
00:37:14,661 --> 00:37:15,864
He's not exactly hiding.

554
00:37:15,913 --> 00:37:17,030
Captain,

555
00:37:17,497 --> 00:37:18,528
you're up.

556
00:39:54,112 --> 00:39:55,315
Kneel before me.

557
00:39:59,701 --> 00:40:01,076
I said

558
00:40:03,080 --> 00:40:05,056
kneel!

559
00:40:14,549 --> 00:40:18,072
ls not this simpler?

560
00:40:19,513 --> 00:40:22,820
Is this not your natural state?

561
00:40:25,018 --> 00:40:28,326
It's the unspoken truth of humanity,

562
00:40:28,396 --> 00:40:30,889
that you crave subjugation.

563
00:40:31,358 --> 00:40:35,267
The bright lure of freedom
diminishes your life's joy

564
00:40:35,320 --> 00:40:37,855
in a mad scramble for power,

565
00:40:39,741 --> 00:40:41,245
for identity.

566
00:40:42,786 --> 00:40:46,309
You were made to be ruled.

567
00:40:46,498 --> 00:40:48,174
In the end,

568
00:40:48,667 --> 00:40:50,729
you will always kneel.

569
00:40:58,343 --> 00:41:00,104
Not to men like you.

570
00:41:01,346 --> 00:41:03,064
There are no men like me.

571
00:41:04,099 --> 00:41:06,935
There are always men like you.

572
00:41:08,270 --> 00:41:09,945
Look to your elder, people.

573
00:41:12,315 --> 00:41:13,647
Let him be an example.

574
00:41:20,574 --> 00:41:23,238
You know, the last time
I was in Germany,

575
00:41:23,326 --> 00:41:26,678
and saw a man standing
above everybody else,

576
00:41:26,746 --> 00:41:28,293
we ended up disagreeing.

577
00:41:28,415 --> 00:41:30,133
The soldier.

578
00:41:32,252 --> 00:41:33,584
The man out of time.

579
00:41:33,920 --> 00:41:35,295
I'm not the one who's out of time.

580
00:41:38,967 --> 00:41:41,330
Loki, drop the weapon
and stand down.

581
00:42:01,907 --> 00:42:03,582
Kneel.

582
00:42:03,617 --> 00:42:04,862
Not today!

583
00:42:06,953 --> 00:42:08,199
The guy's all over the place.

584
00:42:11,875 --> 00:42:14,109
Agent Romanoff. You miss me?

585
00:42:30,977 --> 00:42:33,168
Make your move, Reindeer Games.

586
00:42:41,321 --> 00:42:42,352
Good move.

587
00:42:44,032 --> 00:42:45,407
Mr Stark.

588
00:42:45,992 --> 00:42:47,238
Captain.

589
00:42:54,376 --> 00:42:56,094
Is he saying anything?

590
00:42:56,211 --> 00:42:57,242
Not a word.

591
00:42:57,754 --> 00:42:59,644
Just get him here. We're low on time.

592
00:43:02,592 --> 00:43:03,623
I don't like it.

593
00:43:04,010 --> 00:43:06,072
What, Rock of Ages
giving up so easily?

594
00:43:06,137 --> 00:43:07,898
I don't remember it being that easy.

595
00:43:08,139 --> 00:43:09,643
This guy packs a wallop.

596
00:43:09,766 --> 00:43:13,504
Still, you are pretty spry
for an older fellow.

597
00:43:14,396 --> 00:43:15,985
What's your thing, Pilates?

598
00:43:16,022 --> 00:43:17,053
What?

599
00:43:17,232 --> 00:43:18,306
It's like calisthenics.

600
00:43:18,358 --> 00:43:20,420
You might have missed
a couple of things

601
00:43:20,443 --> 00:43:22,162
doing time as a Capsicle.

602
00:43:24,239 --> 00:43:25,914
Fury didn't tell me
he was calling you in.

603
00:43:26,032 --> 00:43:28,824
Yeah, there's a lot of things
Fury doesn't tell you.

604
00:43:29,119 --> 00:43:30,794
Where's this coming from?

605
00:43:34,624 --> 00:43:37,374
What's the matter? Are you
scared of a little lightning?

606
00:43:37,711 --> 00:43:40,116
I'm not overly fond of what follows.

607
00:43:57,856 --> 00:43:59,101
What are you doing?

608
00:44:12,203 --> 00:44:13,707
And now there's that guy.

609
00:44:13,830 --> 00:44:15,677
Another Asgardian?

610
00:44:15,790 --> 00:44:17,723
- That guy's a friendly?
- Doesn't matter.

611
00:44:17,834 --> 00:44:20,541
If he frees Loki or kills him,
the Tesseract's lost.

612
00:44:20,628 --> 00:44:22,433
Stark, we need a plan of attack!

613
00:44:22,714 --> 00:44:24,905
I have a plan. Attack.

614
00:44:30,972 --> 00:44:32,733
I'd sit this one out, Cap.

615
00:44:32,974 --> 00:44:34,048
I don't see how I can.

616
00:44:34,184 --> 00:44:36,761
These guys come from legend.
They're basically gods.

617
00:44:37,270 --> 00:44:38,645
There's only one God, ma'am.

618
00:44:38,688 --> 00:44:41,180
And I'm pretty sure
he doesn't dress like that.

619
00:44:56,539 --> 00:44:57,829
Where is the Tesseract?

620
00:44:58,124 --> 00:44:59,499
I missed you, too.

621
00:44:59,834 --> 00:45:01,166
Do I look to be in a gaming mood?

622
00:45:01,753 --> 00:45:03,170
You should thank me.

623
00:45:03,838 --> 00:45:06,029
With the Bifrost gone,
how much dark energy

624
00:45:06,132 --> 00:45:08,968
did the Allfather have to
muster to conjure you here

625
00:45:09,052 --> 00:45:10,255
to your precious Earth?

626
00:45:14,391 --> 00:45:15,765
I thought you dead.

627
00:45:17,310 --> 00:45:18,814
Did you mourn?

628
00:45:19,354 --> 00:45:21,029
We all did. Our father...

629
00:45:21,481 --> 00:45:24,273
Your father.

630
00:45:26,319 --> 00:45:29,283
He did tell you
my true parentage, did he not?

631
00:45:31,699 --> 00:45:34,062
We were raised together.

632
00:45:34,160 --> 00:45:36,910
We played together,
we fought together.

633
00:45:37,330 --> 00:45:38,576
Do you remember none of that?

634
00:45:38,706 --> 00:45:40,768
I remember a shadow.

635
00:45:42,168 --> 00:45:44,960
Living in the shade of your greatness.

636
00:45:45,922 --> 00:45:48,671
I remember you tossing me
into an abyss.

637
00:45:48,675 --> 00:45:50,779
I, who was, and should be, king!

638
00:45:51,177 --> 00:45:53,067
So you take the world I love
as a recompense

639
00:45:53,096 --> 00:45:55,072
for your imagined slights?

640
00:45:55,181 --> 00:45:58,361
No. The Earth is under
my protection, Loki.

641
00:45:59,686 --> 00:46:03,080
And you're doing
a marvelous job with that.

642
00:46:03,690 --> 00:46:05,794
The humans slaughter
each other in droves

643
00:46:05,817 --> 00:46:07,707
while you idly fret.

644
00:46:07,735 --> 00:46:10,012
I mean to rule them,
as why should I not?

645
00:46:10,113 --> 00:46:11,445
You think yourself above them?

646
00:46:12,782 --> 00:46:13,813
Well, yes.

647
00:46:13,950 --> 00:46:16,528
Then you miss the truth
of ruling, brother.

648
00:46:16,953 --> 00:46:18,414
A throne would suit you ill.

649
00:46:23,877 --> 00:46:26,454
I've seen worlds
you've never known about!

650
00:46:26,713 --> 00:46:30,966
I have grown, Odinson, in my exile.

651
00:46:31,384 --> 00:46:33,446
I have seen the true power
of the Tesseract,

652
00:46:33,678 --> 00:46:34,679
and when I Wield it...

653
00:46:34,721 --> 00:46:36,611
Who showed you this power?

654
00:46:37,557 --> 00:46:39,018
Who controls the would-be king?

655
00:46:39,225 --> 00:46:41,115
- I am a king!
- Not here!

656
00:46:41,227 --> 00:46:42,559
You give up the Tesseract!

657
00:46:42,604 --> 00:46:45,310
You give up this poisonous dream!

658
00:46:47,692 --> 00:46:49,109
You come home.

659
00:46:53,990 --> 00:46:55,193
I don't have it.

660
00:46:57,202 --> 00:46:59,435
You need the Cube to bring me home.

661
00:46:59,579 --> 00:47:01,512
But I've sent it off, I know not where.

662
00:47:02,790 --> 00:47:04,767
You listen well, brother.

663
00:47:06,252 --> 00:47:07,584
I'm listening.

664
00:47:16,930 --> 00:47:18,433
Do not touch me again.

665
00:47:18,598 --> 00:47:20,231
Then don't take my stuff.

666
00:47:20,266 --> 00:47:22,672
You have no idea
what you're dealing with.

667
00:47:24,479 --> 00:47:25,510
Shakespeare in the Park?

668
00:47:26,940 --> 00:47:30,204
Doth Mother know
you wear-eth her drapes?

669
00:47:30,485 --> 00:47:33,363
This is beyond you, metal man.

670
00:47:33,446 --> 00:47:35,294
Loki will face Asgardian justice.

671
00:47:35,782 --> 00:47:39,261
He gives up the Cube,
he's all yours. Until then,

672
00:47:39,285 --> 00:47:40,575
stay out of the way.

673
00:47:42,330 --> 00:47:43,963
Tourist.

674
00:47:49,128 --> 00:47:50,246
Okay.

675
00:48:20,159 --> 00:48:23,252
Power at 400% capacity.

676
00:48:23,329 --> 00:48:24,619
How about that?

677
00:49:24,932 --> 00:49:26,264
Hey!

678
00:49:28,895 --> 00:49:30,227
That's enough.

679
00:49:33,858 --> 00:49:35,576
Now, I don't know
what you plan on doing here.

680
00:49:35,610 --> 00:49:38,230
I've come here to put an end
to Loki's schemes.

681
00:49:38,237 --> 00:49:40,772
Then prove it. Put that hammer down.

682
00:49:40,782 --> 00:49:41,813
Yeah... No.

683
00:49:42,033 --> 00:49:43,537
Bad call. He loves his hammer.

684
00:49:45,411 --> 00:49:47,473
You want me to put the hammer down?

685
00:50:14,982 --> 00:50:16,744
Are we done, here?

686
00:51:04,532 --> 00:51:07,625
In case it's unclear,

687
00:51:08,202 --> 00:51:10,092
if you try to escape,

688
00:51:11,122 --> 00:51:13,270
if you so much as scratch that glass,

689
00:51:23,009 --> 00:51:26,832
it's 30,000 feet straight down
in a steel trap.

690
00:51:27,513 --> 00:51:29,747
You get how that works?

691
00:51:31,684 --> 00:51:34,433
Ant, boot.

692
00:51:37,648 --> 00:51:39,238
It's an impressive cage.

693
00:51:40,318 --> 00:51:42,766
Not built, I think, for me.

694
00:51:43,279 --> 00:51:45,256
Built for something
a lot stronger than you.

695
00:51:45,907 --> 00:51:47,926
Oh, I've heard.

696
00:51:48,534 --> 00:51:49,780
A mindless beast.

697
00:51:50,995 --> 00:51:52,412
Makes play he's still a man.

698
00:51:53,706 --> 00:51:56,026
How desperate are you,

699
00:51:56,125 --> 00:51:59,347
that you call on such
lost creatures to defend you?

700
00:51:59,420 --> 00:52:01,611
How desperate am I?

701
00:52:01,964 --> 00:52:03,897
You threaten my world with war.

702
00:52:04,008 --> 00:52:06,242
You steal a force
you can't hope to control.

703
00:52:06,344 --> 00:52:10,296
You talk about peace,
and you kill because it's fun.

704
00:52:10,348 --> 00:52:13,483
You have made me very desperate.

705
00:52:13,559 --> 00:52:15,364
You might not be glad that you did.

706
00:52:18,731 --> 00:52:22,168
It burns you to have come so close.

707
00:52:23,444 --> 00:52:25,979
To have the Tesseract, to have power,

708
00:52:26,948 --> 00:52:29,311
unlimited power.

709
00:52:29,408 --> 00:52:31,470
And for what?

710
00:52:32,995 --> 00:52:36,733
A warm light for all mankind to share.

711
00:52:37,083 --> 00:52:40,305
And then to be reminded
what real power is.

712
00:52:44,423 --> 00:52:48,634
Well, let me know if "real power"
wants a magazine or something.

713
00:52:56,978 --> 00:52:58,524
He really grows on you, doesn't he?

714
00:52:58,688 --> 00:53:00,664
Loki's gonna drag this out.

715
00:53:00,773 --> 00:53:04,382
So, Thor, what's his play?

716
00:53:04,443 --> 00:53:07,150
He has an army called the Chitauri.

717
00:53:07,238 --> 00:53:10,245
They're not of Asgard,
nor any world known.

718
00:53:10,575 --> 00:53:12,766
He means to lead them
against your people.

719
00:53:12,869 --> 00:53:14,544
They Will Win him the Earth,

720
00:53:14,579 --> 00:53:16,469
in return, I suspect, for the Tesseract.

721
00:53:16,581 --> 00:53:18,385
An army

722
00:53:18,499 --> 00:53:20,304
from outer space.

723
00:53:20,418 --> 00:53:22,910
So, he's building another portal.

724
00:53:23,004 --> 00:53:24,336
That's what he needs Erik Selvig for.

725
00:53:24,380 --> 00:53:25,411
Selvig?

726
00:53:25,631 --> 00:53:28,123
- He's an astrophysicist.
- He's a friend.

727
00:53:28,217 --> 00:53:30,451
Loki has him under some kind of spell,

728
00:53:30,469 --> 00:53:32,059
along with one of ours.

729
00:53:32,179 --> 00:53:33,898
I want to know why Loki let us take him.

730
00:53:33,931 --> 00:53:35,306
He's not leading an army from here.

731
00:53:35,433 --> 00:53:37,194
I don't think
we should be focusing on Loki.

732
00:53:37,310 --> 00:53:39,242
That guy's brain is a bag full of cats.

733
00:53:39,270 --> 00:53:40,559
You could smell crazy on him.

734
00:53:40,771 --> 00:53:42,490
Have care how you speak.

735
00:53:43,065 --> 00:53:45,042
Loki is beyond reason,
but he is of Asgard.

736
00:53:45,484 --> 00:53:46,645
And he is my brother.

737
00:53:46,903 --> 00:53:48,750
He killed 80 people in two days.

738
00:53:49,655 --> 00:53:50,686
He's adopted.

739
00:53:50,865 --> 00:53:53,270
I think it's about the mechanics.

740
00:53:53,367 --> 00:53:55,429
Iridium... What do they
need the iridium for?

741
00:53:55,494 --> 00:53:56,525
It's a stabilising agent.

742
00:53:56,704 --> 00:53:58,079
I'm just saying, pick a weekend.

743
00:53:58,164 --> 00:53:59,753
I'll fly you to Portland.

744
00:53:59,874 --> 00:54:01,549
Keep love alive.

745
00:54:01,667 --> 00:54:03,644
It means the portal
won't collapse on itself

746
00:54:03,669 --> 00:54:05,646
like it did at S.H.I.E.L.D.

747
00:54:05,755 --> 00:54:09,149
No hard feelings, Point Break.
You've got a mean swing.

748
00:54:09,216 --> 00:54:11,579
Also, it means the portal
can open as wide

749
00:54:11,677 --> 00:54:14,255
and stay open as long, as Loki wants.

750
00:54:14,847 --> 00:54:16,909
Raise the mizzenmast. Jib the topsails.

751
00:54:18,559 --> 00:54:19,805
That man is playing Galaga.

752
00:54:21,020 --> 00:54:24,499
He thought we wouldn't notice,
but we did.

753
00:54:26,192 --> 00:54:27,609
How does Fury even see these?

754
00:54:27,652 --> 00:54:28,725
He turns.

755
00:54:29,195 --> 00:54:30,913
Sounds exhausting.

756
00:54:31,864 --> 00:54:33,153
The rest of the raw materials,

757
00:54:33,282 --> 00:54:36,161
Agent Barton can get
his hands on pretty easily.

758
00:54:36,243 --> 00:54:37,747
The only major component
he still needs

759
00:54:37,870 --> 00:54:41,479
is a power source
of high-energy density.

760
00:54:41,540 --> 00:54:44,763
Something to kick-start the Cube.

761
00:54:45,044 --> 00:54:47,836
When did you become an expert
in thermonuclear astrophysics?

762
00:54:47,838 --> 00:54:48,956
Last night.

763
00:54:49,715 --> 00:54:53,023
The packet, Selvig's notes,
the extraction theory papers.

764
00:54:53,094 --> 00:54:54,167
Am I the only one who did the reading?

765
00:54:54,303 --> 00:54:57,182
Does Loki need any particular
kind of power source?

766
00:54:57,264 --> 00:55:00,143
He would have to heat the Cube
to 120-million Kelvin

767
00:55:00,226 --> 00:55:01,772
just to break through
the Coulomb barrier.

768
00:55:01,894 --> 00:55:04,214
Unless Selvig has figured out
how to stabilise

769
00:55:04,313 --> 00:55:05,473
the quantum tunnelling effect.

770
00:55:05,606 --> 00:55:06,852
Well, if he could do that,

771
00:55:06,899 --> 00:55:09,434
he could achieve heavy ion fusion
at any reactor on the planet.

772
00:55:09,443 --> 00:55:11,978
Finally, someone who speaks English.

773
00:55:12,071 --> 00:55:14,004
Is that what just happened?

774
00:55:14,240 --> 00:55:16,344
It's good to meet you, Dr Banner.

775
00:55:16,450 --> 00:55:19,672
Your work on antielectron
collisions is unparalleled.

776
00:55:19,745 --> 00:55:21,635
And I'm a huge fan of the way
you lose control

777
00:55:21,747 --> 00:55:23,680
and turn into an enormous
green rage-monster.

778
00:55:25,334 --> 00:55:26,452
Thanks.

779
00:55:26,585 --> 00:55:29,163
Dr Banner is only here
to track the Cube.

780
00:55:29,255 --> 00:55:30,629
I was hoping you might join him.

781
00:55:30,756 --> 00:55:31,787
I would start with that stick of his.

782
00:55:32,091 --> 00:55:33,092
It may be magical,

783
00:55:33,134 --> 00:55:34,637
but it works an awful lot
like a HYDRA weapon.

784
00:55:34,677 --> 00:55:37,684
I don't know about that,
but it is powered by the Cube.

785
00:55:37,972 --> 00:55:39,777
And I would like to know
how Loki used it

786
00:55:39,932 --> 00:55:41,650
to turn two of the sharpest men I know

787
00:55:41,684 --> 00:55:43,489
into his personal flying monkeys.

788
00:55:43,811 --> 00:55:45,357
Monkeys? I do not understand.

789
00:55:45,563 --> 00:55:46,564
I do.

790
00:55:49,483 --> 00:55:51,159
I understood that reference.

791
00:55:52,278 --> 00:55:53,695
Shall we play, Doctor?

792
00:55:53,821 --> 00:55:55,497
This way, sir.

793
00:56:09,545 --> 00:56:11,178
The gamma readings
are definitely consistent

794
00:56:11,297 --> 00:56:13,144
with Selvig's reports of the Tesseract.

795
00:56:13,716 --> 00:56:15,434
But it's going to take weeks to process.

796
00:56:15,551 --> 00:56:16,840
If we bypass their mainframe

797
00:56:16,886 --> 00:56:18,218
and direct route to the Homer cluster,

798
00:56:18,345 --> 00:56:21,568
we can clock this
at around 600 teraflops.

799
00:56:22,641 --> 00:56:24,703
All I packed was a toothbrush.

800
00:56:25,644 --> 00:56:27,363
You know, you should come by
Stark Tower sometime.

801
00:56:27,480 --> 00:56:29,542
Top ten floors, all R&D.

802
00:56:29,815 --> 00:56:31,362
You'd love it. It's Candy Land.

803
00:56:31,484 --> 00:56:34,148
Thanks, but the last time
I was in New York,

804
00:56:34,236 --> 00:56:36,900
I kind of broke Harlem.

805
00:56:36,989 --> 00:56:38,879
Well, I promise
a stress-free environment.

806
00:56:38,991 --> 00:56:40,881
No tension, no surprises.

807
00:56:42,328 --> 00:56:43,789
- Hey!
- Nothing?

808
00:56:43,871 --> 00:56:44,945
Are you nuts?

809
00:56:44,997 --> 00:56:46,028
Jury's out.

810
00:56:46,207 --> 00:56:47,452
You really have got
a lid on it, haven't you?

811
00:56:47,500 --> 00:56:48,531
What's your secret?

812
00:56:48,626 --> 00:56:50,130
Mellow jazz, bongo drums
huge bag of weed?

813
00:56:50,169 --> 00:56:51,200
Is everything a joke to you?

814
00:56:51,629 --> 00:56:52,660
Funny things are.

815
00:56:52,838 --> 00:56:54,643
Threatening the safety
of everyone on this ship

816
00:56:54,673 --> 00:56:56,005
isn't funny.

817
00:56:56,050 --> 00:56:57,081
No of fence, Doc.

818
00:56:57,134 --> 00:56:58,810
It's all right,
I wouldn't have come aboard

819
00:56:58,844 --> 00:57:01,805
if I couldn't handle pointy things.

820
00:57:01,806 --> 00:57:04,254
You're tip-toeing, big man.
You need to strut.

821
00:57:04,517 --> 00:57:06,278
And you need to focus
on the problem, Mr Stark.

822
00:57:06,310 --> 00:57:07,727
Do you think I'm not?

823
00:57:07,937 --> 00:57:10,855
Why did Fury call us in?
Why now? Why not before?

824
00:57:10,856 --> 00:57:12,617
What isn't he telling us?

825
00:57:12,650 --> 00:57:14,239
I can't do the equation unless
I have all the variables.

826
00:57:14,819 --> 00:57:16,193
You think Fury's hiding something?

827
00:57:16,487 --> 00:57:19,739
He's a spy. Captain, he's "the" spy.

828
00:57:19,740 --> 00:57:21,630
His secrets have secrets.

829
00:57:21,659 --> 00:57:23,248
It's bugging him, too. Isn't it?

830
00:57:25,371 --> 00:57:26,917
I just want to finish my work here, and...

831
00:57:27,540 --> 00:57:28,571
Doctor?

832
00:57:34,046 --> 00:57:36,538
"A warm light for all mankind."

833
00:57:36,549 --> 00:57:38,611
Loki's jab at Fury about the Cube.

834
00:57:38,759 --> 00:57:40,048
I heard it.

835
00:57:40,094 --> 00:57:42,499
I think that was meant for you.

836
00:57:43,347 --> 00:57:46,432
Even if Barton didn't
tell Loki about the tower,

837
00:57:46,433 --> 00:57:47,507
it was still all over the news.

838
00:57:47,685 --> 00:57:49,704
The Stark Tower? That big, ugly

839
00:57:50,896 --> 00:57:52,142
building in New York?

840
00:57:52,439 --> 00:57:56,276
It's powered by an arc reactor,
a self-sustaining energy source.

841
00:57:56,277 --> 00:57:58,854
That building will run itself
for, what, a year?

842
00:57:58,863 --> 00:58:00,753
It's just the prototype.

843
00:58:00,781 --> 00:58:02,714
I'm kind of the only name
in clean energy right now.

844
00:58:03,075 --> 00:58:04,536
That's what he's getting at.

845
00:58:04,577 --> 00:58:07,326
So, why didn't S.H.I.E.L.D. bring him in
on the Tesseract project?

846
00:58:07,413 --> 00:58:09,260
What are they doing
in the energy business

847
00:58:09,290 --> 00:58:10,622
in the first place?

848
00:58:10,749 --> 00:58:13,842
I should probably look into that
once my decryption programme

849
00:58:13,878 --> 00:58:15,897
finishes breaking into all of
S.H.I.E.L.D.'s secure files.

850
00:58:15,921 --> 00:58:16,922
I'm sorry. Did you say...

851
00:58:16,964 --> 00:58:19,155
Jarvis has been running it
since I hit the bridge.

852
00:58:19,425 --> 00:58:21,058
In a few hours,
I'll know every dirty secret

853
00:58:21,093 --> 00:58:22,382
S.H.I.E.L.D. has ever tried to hide.

854
00:58:22,428 --> 00:58:23,429
Blueberry?

855
00:58:23,470 --> 00:58:25,275
Yet you're confused about why
they didn't want you around.

856
00:58:25,556 --> 00:58:28,263
An intelligence organisation
that fears intelligence?

857
00:58:28,517 --> 00:58:30,193
Historically, not awesome.

858
00:58:30,227 --> 00:58:32,590
I think Loki's trying to wind us up.

859
00:58:32,605 --> 00:58:34,280
This is a man who means to start a war

860
00:58:34,315 --> 00:58:35,818
and if we don't stay focused,
he'll succeed.

861
00:58:37,067 --> 00:58:39,645
We have orders.
We should follow them.

862
00:58:40,112 --> 00:58:42,002
Following's not really my style.

863
00:58:43,324 --> 00:58:45,816
And you're all about style, aren't you?

864
00:58:45,826 --> 00:58:46,944
Of the people in this room,

865
00:58:46,994 --> 00:58:48,712
which one is,
A, wearing a spangly outfit,

866
00:58:48,746 --> 00:58:49,949
and, B, not of use?

867
00:58:50,164 --> 00:58:54,417
Steve, tell me none of this
smells a little funky to you.

868
00:58:57,004 --> 00:58:58,121
Just find the Cube.

869
00:59:10,976 --> 00:59:13,038
That's the guy
my dad never shut up about?

870
00:59:13,604 --> 00:59:16,525
I'm wondering if they shouldn't have
kept him on ice.

871
00:59:17,191 --> 00:59:18,996
The guy's not wrong about Loki.

872
00:59:19,026 --> 00:59:20,916
He does have the jump on us.

873
00:59:20,945 --> 00:59:23,780
What he's got is an Acme dynamite kit.

874
00:59:23,781 --> 00:59:25,671
It's going to blow up in his face.

875
00:59:25,699 --> 00:59:27,890
And I'm going to be there when it does.

876
00:59:28,327 --> 00:59:30,561
Yeah. I'll read all about it.

877
00:59:32,414 --> 00:59:33,789
Or you'll be suiting up
with the rest of us.

878
00:59:35,501 --> 00:59:39,170
You see, I don't get a suit of Armour.

879
00:59:39,171 --> 00:59:42,674
I'm exposed. Like a nerve.

880
00:59:42,675 --> 00:59:44,221
It's a nightmare.

881
00:59:44,510 --> 00:59:47,470
I've got a cluster of shrapnel
trying every second

882
00:59:47,471 --> 00:59:49,576
to crawl its way into my heart.

883
00:59:49,598 --> 00:59:51,747
This stops it.

884
00:59:51,767 --> 00:59:54,001
This little circle of light,
it's part of me now,

885
00:59:55,312 --> 00:59:56,901
not just Armour.

886
00:59:57,648 --> 01:00:00,011
It's a terrible privilege.

887
01:00:00,442 --> 01:00:02,763
- But you can control it.
- Because I learned how.

888
01:00:02,778 --> 01:00:03,809
It's different.

889
01:00:04,280 --> 01:00:07,699
Hey, I read all about your accident.

890
01:00:07,700 --> 01:00:11,007
That much gamma exposure
should have killed you.

891
01:00:11,203 --> 01:00:13,781
So you're saying that the Hulk...

892
01:00:15,124 --> 01:00:17,358
The other guy saved my life?

893
01:00:17,793 --> 01:00:18,996
That's nice.

894
01:00:20,004 --> 01:00:23,827
It's a nice sentiment. Saved it for what?

895
01:00:25,050 --> 01:00:26,940
I guess we'll find out.

896
01:00:28,721 --> 01:00:30,482
You may not enjoy that.

897
01:00:30,514 --> 01:00:32,576
And you just might.

898
01:01:31,700 --> 01:01:33,161
As soon as Loki took the doctor,

899
01:01:33,452 --> 01:01:35,041
we moved Jane Foster.

900
01:01:35,079 --> 01:01:37,571
They've got an excellent
observatory in Troms?.

901
01:01:37,581 --> 01:01:41,250
She was asked to consult there
very suddenly yesterday.

902
01:01:41,251 --> 01:01:45,204
Handsome fee, private plane,
very remote.

903
01:01:45,798 --> 01:01:46,915
She'll be safe.

904
01:01:47,091 --> 01:01:48,508
Thank you.

905
01:01:50,260 --> 01:01:52,151
It's no accident, Loki taking Erik Selvig.

906
01:01:53,305 --> 01:01:55,797
I dread what he plans for him
once he's done.

907
01:01:55,808 --> 01:01:57,010
Erik is a good man.

908
01:01:57,059 --> 01:01:58,133
He talks about you a lot.

909
01:02:00,145 --> 01:02:02,207
You changed his life.

910
01:02:03,816 --> 01:02:05,792
You changed everything around here.

911
01:02:05,818 --> 01:02:08,051
They were better as they were.

912
01:02:08,570 --> 01:02:10,761
We pretend on Asgard
that we're more advanced

913
01:02:10,781 --> 01:02:14,617
but we come here,
battling like bilge snipe.

914
01:02:14,618 --> 01:02:16,551
- Like what?
- Bilge snipe.

915
01:02:16,578 --> 01:02:19,414
You know, huge, scaly, big antlers.

916
01:02:20,416 --> 01:02:22,306
- You don't have those?
- I don't think so.

917
01:02:22,334 --> 01:02:24,311
Well, they are repulsive.

918
01:02:25,504 --> 01:02:27,910
And they trample everything
in their path.

919
01:02:35,472 --> 01:02:38,866
When I first came to Earth,
Loki's rage followed me here,

920
01:02:38,934 --> 01:02:41,168
and your people paid the price.

921
01:02:41,353 --> 01:02:43,243
And now, again.

922
01:02:45,691 --> 01:02:48,268
In my youth, I courted war.

923
01:02:49,945 --> 01:02:52,050
War hasn't started yet.

924
01:02:53,073 --> 01:02:54,963
You think you could make Loki tell us

925
01:02:54,992 --> 01:02:56,324
where the Tesseract is?

926
01:02:56,368 --> 01:02:59,787
I do not know. Loki's mind is far afield.

927
01:02:59,788 --> 01:03:04,625
It's not just power he craves,
it's vengeance, upon me.

928
01:03:04,626 --> 01:03:06,517
There's no pain
would prise his need from him.

929
01:03:07,838 --> 01:03:10,158
A lot of guys think that

930
01:03:10,174 --> 01:03:11,463
until the pain starts.

931
01:03:13,969 --> 01:03:15,516
What are you asking me to do?

932
01:03:15,554 --> 01:03:19,162
I'm asking,
what are you prepared to do?

933
01:03:19,224 --> 01:03:20,255
Loki is a prisoner.

934
01:03:20,476 --> 01:03:22,881
Then why do I feel like
he's the only person on this boat

935
01:03:22,895 --> 01:03:24,312
that wants to be here?

936
01:03:37,075 --> 01:03:40,328
There's not many people
who can sneak up on me.

937
01:03:40,329 --> 01:03:41,962
But you figured I'd come.

938
01:03:42,664 --> 01:03:44,125
After.

939
01:03:45,083 --> 01:03:48,669
After whatever tortures
Fury can concoct,

940
01:03:48,670 --> 01:03:52,493
you would appear
as a friend, as a balm.

941
01:03:53,258 --> 01:03:54,891
And I would cooperate.

942
01:03:55,093 --> 01:03:57,026
I want to know what
you've done to Agent Barton.

943
01:03:57,221 --> 01:03:59,111
I would say I've expanded his mind.

944
01:04:01,767 --> 01:04:03,829
And once you've won,

945
01:04:04,269 --> 01:04:05,644
once you're king of the mountain,

946
01:04:08,023 --> 01:04:10,643
what happens to his mind?

947
01:04:11,777 --> 01:04:13,452
Is this love, Agent Romanoff?

948
01:04:13,695 --> 01:04:16,402
Love is for children. I owe him a debt.

949
01:04:20,410 --> 01:04:22,171
Tell me.

950
01:04:26,625 --> 01:04:30,019
Before I worked for S.H.I.E.L.D... I...

951
01:04:32,297 --> 01:04:36,300
Well, I made a name for myself.

952
01:04:36,301 --> 01:04:39,470
I have a very specific skill set.

953
01:04:39,471 --> 01:04:42,994
I didn't care who I used it for, or on.

954
01:04:44,142 --> 01:04:47,536
I got on S.H.I.E.L.D.'s radar
in a bad way.

955
01:04:48,814 --> 01:04:51,864
Agent Barton was sent to kill me.

956
01:04:52,776 --> 01:04:54,193
He made a different call.

957
01:04:56,280 --> 01:04:59,243
And what will you do
if I vow to spare him?

958
01:04:59,575 --> 01:05:01,036
Not let you out.

959
01:05:01,076 --> 01:05:03,053
No, but I like this.

960
01:05:03,954 --> 01:05:07,305
Your world in the balance,
and you bargain for one man.

961
01:05:07,499 --> 01:05:09,648
Regimes fall every day.

962
01:05:09,668 --> 01:05:12,116
I tend not to weep over that.
I'm Russian.

963
01:05:12,129 --> 01:05:13,202
Or I was.

964
01:05:14,673 --> 01:05:16,219
And what are you now?

965
01:05:16,800 --> 01:05:19,885
It's really not that complicated.

966
01:05:19,886 --> 01:05:24,140
I got red in my ledger,
I'd like to wipe it out.

967
01:05:24,975 --> 01:05:26,392
Can you?

968
01:05:27,853 --> 01:05:31,805
Can you wipe out that much red?

969
01:05:32,816 --> 01:05:34,405
Dreykov's daughter,

970
01:05:36,028 --> 01:05:37,960
São Paulo,

971
01:05:38,905 --> 01:05:41,311
the hospital fire?

972
01:05:42,242 --> 01:05:44,691
Barton told me everything.

973
01:05:44,703 --> 01:05:47,667
Your ledger is dripping. It's gushing red

974
01:05:47,831 --> 01:05:50,580
and you think saving a man
no more virtuous than yourself

975
01:05:50,584 --> 01:05:52,001
will change anything?

976
01:05:52,044 --> 01:05:54,879
This is the basest sentimentality.

977
01:05:54,880 --> 01:05:57,200
This is a child at prayer.

978
01:05:57,215 --> 01:05:58,418
Pathetic!

979
01:05:59,343 --> 01:06:02,049
You lie and kill

980
01:06:02,054 --> 01:06:05,233
in the service of liars and killers.

981
01:06:08,185 --> 01:06:11,320
You pretend to be separate,
to have your own code,

982
01:06:11,480 --> 01:06:14,315
something that makes up
for the horrors.

983
01:06:15,359 --> 01:06:17,893
But they are part of you.

984
01:06:17,903 --> 01:06:21,598
And they will never go away.

985
01:06:22,282 --> 01:06:25,910
I won't touch Barton,
not until I make him kill you.

986
01:06:25,911 --> 01:06:28,231
Slowly, intimately,

987
01:06:28,246 --> 01:06:30,781
in every way he knows you fear.

988
01:06:30,791 --> 01:06:33,712
And then he'll wake just long
enough to see his good work

989
01:06:34,002 --> 01:06:37,611
and when he screams, I'll split his skull.

990
01:06:37,673 --> 01:06:40,508
This is my bargain, you mewling quim.

991
01:06:42,260 --> 01:06:43,979
You're a monster.

992
01:06:46,098 --> 01:06:47,644
Oh, no.

993
01:06:48,475 --> 01:06:49,807
You brought the monster.

994
01:06:53,063 --> 01:06:54,480
So, Banner.

995
01:06:55,440 --> 01:06:56,643
That's your play.

996
01:06:56,858 --> 01:06:57,889
What?

997
01:06:58,860 --> 01:07:00,536
Loki means to unleash the Hulk.

998
01:07:00,570 --> 01:07:02,160
Keep Banner in the lab. I'm on my way.

999
01:07:02,197 --> 01:07:03,314
Send Thor as well.

1000
01:07:05,325 --> 01:07:06,356
Thank you

1001
01:07:06,576 --> 01:07:08,853
for your cooperation.

1002
01:07:16,253 --> 01:07:17,757
What are you doing, Mr Stark?

1003
01:07:17,796 --> 01:07:20,460
Kind of been wondering
the same thing about you.

1004
01:07:20,799 --> 01:07:22,432
You're supposed to be locating
the Tesseract.

1005
01:07:22,467 --> 01:07:23,799
We are. The model's locked

1006
01:07:23,969 --> 01:07:25,558
and we're sweeping
for the signature now.

1007
01:07:25,595 --> 01:07:26,927
When we get a hit,

1008
01:07:26,972 --> 01:07:28,518
we'll have the location
within half a mile.

1009
01:07:28,807 --> 01:07:33,144
Yeah, then you get your
Cube back. No muss, no fuss.

1010
01:07:33,145 --> 01:07:34,218
What is "Phase 2"?

1011
01:07:36,523 --> 01:07:39,483
Phase 2 is S.H.I.E.L.D. uses
the Cube to make weapons.

1012
01:07:39,484 --> 01:07:41,332
Sorry, computer was moving
a little slow for me.

1013
01:07:41,653 --> 01:07:44,145
Rogers, we gathered everything
related to the Tesseract.

1014
01:07:44,156 --> 01:07:45,488
This does not mean that we're making...

1015
01:07:45,532 --> 01:07:46,563
I'm sorry, Nick.

1016
01:07:46,616 --> 01:07:49,065
What were you lying?

1017
01:07:49,077 --> 01:07:50,409
I was wrong, Director.

1018
01:07:50,495 --> 01:07:51,613
The world hasn't changed a bit.

1019
01:07:51,663 --> 01:07:52,694
Did you know about this?

1020
01:07:52,998 --> 01:07:54,716
You want to think about
removing yourself

1021
01:07:54,750 --> 01:07:55,910
from this environment, Doctor?

1022
01:07:55,959 --> 01:07:57,892
I was in Calcutta.
I was pretty well removed.

1023
01:07:58,128 --> 01:07:59,503
Loki is manipulating you.

1024
01:07:59,671 --> 01:08:01,088
And you've been doing what, exactly?

1025
01:08:01,131 --> 01:08:02,720
You didn't come here because
I bat my eyelashes at you.

1026
01:08:02,758 --> 01:08:04,047
Yes, and I'm not leaving

1027
01:08:04,092 --> 01:08:05,510
because suddenly
you get a little twitchy.

1028
01:08:05,719 --> 01:08:07,437
I'd like to know Why S.H.I.E.L.D.

1029
01:08:07,471 --> 01:08:11,208
is using the Tesseract
to build weapons of mass destruction.

1030
01:08:11,808 --> 01:08:13,011
Because of him.

1031
01:08:13,852 --> 01:08:14,883
Me?

1032
01:08:16,188 --> 01:08:18,680
Last year, Earth had a visitor
from another planet

1033
01:08:18,690 --> 01:08:21,984
who had a grudge match
that levelled a small town.

1034
01:08:21,985 --> 01:08:24,176
We learned that
not only are we not alone

1035
01:08:24,321 --> 01:08:28,032
but we are hopelessly,
hilariously, outgunned.

1036
01:08:28,033 --> 01:08:30,224
My people want nothing
but peace with your planet.

1037
01:08:30,368 --> 01:08:32,473
But you're not the only people
out there, are you?

1038
01:08:32,496 --> 01:08:34,428
And you're not the only threat.

1039
01:08:34,539 --> 01:08:37,632
The world's filling up with
people who can't be matched,

1040
01:08:38,210 --> 01:08:39,584
that can't be controlled.

1041
01:08:39,753 --> 01:08:40,956
Like you controlled the Cube?

1042
01:08:41,004 --> 01:08:42,336
Your work with the Tesseract

1043
01:08:42,380 --> 01:08:45,044
is what drew Loki to it, and his allies.

1044
01:08:45,050 --> 01:08:46,554
It is a signal to all the realms

1045
01:08:46,593 --> 01:08:49,385
that the Earth is ready
for a higher form of war.

1046
01:08:49,387 --> 01:08:50,505
A higher form?

1047
01:08:50,555 --> 01:08:51,715
You forced our hand.

1048
01:08:51,765 --> 01:08:52,796
We had to come up with something.

1049
01:08:52,849 --> 01:08:53,880
A nuclear deterrent.

1050
01:08:53,934 --> 01:08:56,082
Because that always
calms everything right down.

1051
01:08:56,102 --> 01:08:58,595
Remind me again how
you made your fortune, Stark.

1052
01:08:58,605 --> 01:09:00,839
I'm sure if he still made weapons,
Stark would be neck-deep...

1053
01:09:01,066 --> 01:09:02,827
Hold on. How is this now about me?

1054
01:09:02,859 --> 01:09:04,019
I'm sorry, isn't everything?

1055
01:09:04,069 --> 01:09:06,088
I thought humans were
more evolved than this.

1056
01:09:06,112 --> 01:09:09,114
Excuse me, did we come to
your planet and blow stuff up?

1057
01:09:09,115 --> 01:09:11,048
You treat your champions
with such mistrust.

1058
01:09:11,076 --> 01:09:12,665
Are you boys really that naïve?

1059
01:09:12,702 --> 01:09:14,679
S.H.I.E.L.D. monitors potential threats.

1060
01:09:14,704 --> 01:09:16,079
Captain America's on threat watch?

1061
01:09:16,122 --> 01:09:17,153
We all are.

1062
01:09:17,207 --> 01:09:18,753
Wait, you're on that list?

1063
01:09:18,792 --> 01:09:20,425
Are you above or below angry bees?

1064
01:09:20,460 --> 01:09:22,694
Stark, so help me God,
if you make one more wisecrack...

1065
01:09:22,712 --> 01:09:24,044
Threat! Verbal threat. I feel threatened.

1066
01:09:24,089 --> 01:09:26,666
- Show some respect.
- Respect what?

1067
01:09:33,932 --> 01:09:36,976
Transport Six-Six-Bravo,
please relay confirm codes.

1068
01:09:36,977 --> 01:09:39,253
I've got you on the computer,
but not on the day log.

1069
01:09:39,271 --> 01:09:41,419
What is your haul? Over.

1070
01:09:41,439 --> 01:09:43,932
Arms and ammunition. Over.

1071
01:09:52,450 --> 01:09:54,771
You speak of control,
yet you court chaos.

1072
01:09:54,786 --> 01:09:56,419
That's his M.O., isn't it?

1073
01:09:56,621 --> 01:09:57,911
I mean, what are we, a team?

1074
01:09:57,956 --> 01:10:01,083
No, we're a chemical mixture
that makes chaos.

1075
01:10:01,084 --> 01:10:02,845
We're a time bomb.

1076
01:10:03,128 --> 01:10:05,104
You need to step away.

1077
01:10:05,130 --> 01:10:07,063
Why shouldn't the guy
let off a little steam?

1078
01:10:07,090 --> 01:10:09,281
You know damn well why. Back off!

1079
01:10:09,301 --> 01:10:11,621
I'm starting to want you to make me.

1080
01:10:11,636 --> 01:10:15,374
Yeah. Big man in a suit of Armour.

1081
01:10:15,432 --> 01:10:16,721
Take that off, what are you?

1082
01:10:16,975 --> 01:10:19,338
Genius, billionaire,
playboy, philanthropist.

1083
01:10:20,228 --> 01:10:23,314
I know guys with none of that
worth ten of you.

1084
01:10:23,315 --> 01:10:24,432
I've seen the footage.

1085
01:10:24,649 --> 01:10:26,711
The only thing you really
fight for is yourself.

1086
01:10:28,278 --> 01:10:30,297
You're not the guy
to make the sacrifice play,

1087
01:10:30,405 --> 01:10:32,811
to lay down on a wire and let
the other guy crawl over you.

1088
01:10:32,991 --> 01:10:34,968
I think I would just cut the wire.

1089
01:10:37,787 --> 01:10:40,108
Always a way out.

1090
01:10:40,123 --> 01:10:41,455
You may not be a threat

1091
01:10:41,499 --> 01:10:43,390
but you better stop pretending
to be a hero.

1092
01:10:43,501 --> 01:10:46,122
A hero? Like you?

1093
01:10:46,129 --> 01:10:48,277
You're a laboratory experiment, Rogers.

1094
01:10:48,298 --> 01:10:51,821
Everything special about you
came out of a bottle.

1095
01:11:17,202 --> 01:11:19,866
Put on the suit. Let's go a few rounds.

1096
01:11:21,039 --> 01:11:24,647
You people are so petty and tiny.

1097
01:11:24,834 --> 01:11:25,694
Yeah, this is a team.

1098
01:11:25,752 --> 01:11:26,912
Agent Romanoff, would you escort

1099
01:11:26,962 --> 01:11:28,035
Dr Banner back to his...

1100
01:11:28,171 --> 01:11:29,889
Where? You rented my room.

1101
01:11:30,173 --> 01:11:31,849
The cell was just in case...

1102
01:11:32,050 --> 01:11:33,339
In case you needed to kill me.

1103
01:11:33,385 --> 01:11:36,134
But you can't. I know, I tried.

1104
01:11:39,057 --> 01:11:42,059
I got low. I didn't see an end.

1105
01:11:42,060 --> 01:11:46,570
So, I put a bullet in my mouth,
and the other guy spit it out.

1106
01:11:47,148 --> 01:11:48,438
So I moved on.

1107
01:11:48,483 --> 01:11:51,147
I focused on helping
other people. I was good.

1108
01:11:51,403 --> 01:11:53,636
Until you dragged me back
into this freak show

1109
01:11:53,738 --> 01:11:54,941
and put everyone here at risk.

1110
01:11:55,281 --> 01:11:57,473
You want to know my secret,
Agent Romanoff?

1111
01:11:57,492 --> 01:11:59,125
You want to know how I stay calm?

1112
01:12:02,122 --> 01:12:04,141
Dr Banner,

1113
01:12:04,958 --> 01:12:06,375
put down the sceptre.

1114
01:12:15,176 --> 01:12:16,422
Got it.

1115
01:12:16,928 --> 01:12:18,002
Sorry, kids,

1116
01:12:18,096 --> 01:12:19,986
you don't get to see
my party trick after all.

1117
01:12:20,056 --> 01:12:21,130
You located the Tesseract?

1118
01:12:21,224 --> 01:12:22,255
I could get there fastest.

1119
01:12:22,392 --> 01:12:24,540
The Tesseract belongs on Asgard.
No human is a match for it.

1120
01:12:24,686 --> 01:12:25,931
- You're not going alone.
- You're gonna stop me?

1121
01:12:26,021 --> 01:12:27,094
Put on the suit, let's find out.

1122
01:12:27,230 --> 01:12:28,476
I'm not afraid to hit an old man.

1123
01:12:28,523 --> 01:12:29,554
Put on the suit.

1124
01:12:32,569 --> 01:12:33,986
Oh, my God.

1125
01:12:49,711 --> 01:12:50,742
Put on the suit.

1126
01:12:50,795 --> 01:12:52,170
Yeah.

1127
01:12:54,883 --> 01:12:56,687
All hands to stations.

1128
01:13:00,764 --> 01:13:02,525
- Hill!
- External detonation.

1129
01:13:02,682 --> 01:13:04,014
Number three engine is down.

1130
01:13:04,059 --> 01:13:05,090
We've been hit.

1131
01:13:05,143 --> 01:13:06,432
- Can they get it running?
- Fire in engine three!

1132
01:13:06,478 --> 01:13:07,509
Talk to me.

1133
01:13:07,562 --> 01:13:09,323
Turbine looks mostly intact

1134
01:13:09,355 --> 01:13:11,332
but it's impossible to
get out there to make repairs

1135
01:13:11,357 --> 01:13:12,861
while we're in the air.

1136
01:13:12,901 --> 01:13:15,565
If we lose one more engine,
we won't be.

1137
01:13:15,570 --> 01:13:17,675
Somebody's got to get outside
and patch that engine.

1138
01:13:17,697 --> 01:13:19,201
- Stark, you copy that?
- I'm on it.

1139
01:13:19,532 --> 01:13:22,743
Coulson, initiate defensive lockdown
in the detention section

1140
01:13:22,744 --> 01:13:23,861
then get to the armoury.

1141
01:13:23,953 --> 01:13:25,027
Romanoff?

1142
01:13:28,833 --> 01:13:30,036
We're okay.

1143
01:13:32,629 --> 01:13:33,961
We're okay, right?

1144
01:13:46,726 --> 01:13:48,015
- Keep that engine down!
- Yes, sir.

1145
01:13:48,061 --> 01:13:49,822
Detention, wait for cameras to go dark.

1146
01:13:49,854 --> 01:13:51,787
- Got it.
- Stay close.

1147
01:13:53,441 --> 01:13:55,030
Let's go, Level 4.

1148
01:13:55,860 --> 01:13:58,567
Engine three. I'll meet you there.

1149
01:14:06,871 --> 01:14:08,117
Doctor?

1150
01:14:10,041 --> 01:14:11,072
Bruce?

1151
01:14:11,709 --> 01:14:15,233
You got to fight it.
This is just what Loki wants.

1152
01:14:16,464 --> 01:14:17,667
We're going to be okay. Listen to me.

1153
01:14:17,715 --> 01:14:18,746
Are you hurt?

1154
01:14:22,220 --> 01:14:24,239
We're going to be okay. All right?

1155
01:14:24,556 --> 01:14:27,477
I swear on my life,
I will get you out of this.

1156
01:14:27,684 --> 01:14:28,887
You will walk away and never ever...

1157
01:14:28,935 --> 01:14:30,825
Your life?

1158
01:14:47,245 --> 01:14:48,276
Bruce.

1159
01:15:25,408 --> 01:15:28,702
Bring the carrier about
to a 1-8-0, heading south!

1160
01:15:28,703 --> 01:15:30,593
- Take us to the water!
- We're flying blind.

1161
01:15:30,705 --> 01:15:32,682
Navigation's recalibrating
after the engine failure.

1162
01:15:32,790 --> 01:15:34,337
Is the sun coming up?

1163
01:15:35,335 --> 01:15:37,354
- Yes, sir.
- Then put it on the left.

1164
01:15:37,629 --> 01:15:39,175
Get us over water.

1165
01:15:39,464 --> 01:15:41,311
One more turbine goes down,
and we drop.

1166
01:15:43,801 --> 01:15:45,176
Thanks.

1167
01:15:48,431 --> 01:15:49,677
Stark!

1168
01:15:52,310 --> 01:15:54,071
Stark, I'm here!

1169
01:15:54,103 --> 01:15:55,349
Good.

1170
01:15:56,814 --> 01:15:58,919
Let's see what we've got.

1171
01:15:58,942 --> 01:16:00,617
I got to get this
superconducting coolant system

1172
01:16:00,735 --> 01:16:01,766
back online

1173
01:16:01,819 --> 01:16:03,409
before I can access the rotors,

1174
01:16:03,446 --> 01:16:05,079
work on dislodging the debris.

1175
01:16:07,533 --> 01:16:09,209
I need you to get to that
engine control panel

1176
01:16:09,327 --> 01:16:13,065
and tell me which relays
are in overload position.

1177
01:16:25,468 --> 01:16:26,885
What does it look like in there?

1178
01:16:27,720 --> 01:16:30,126
It seems to run
on some form of electricity.

1179
01:16:30,348 --> 01:16:31,981
Well, you're not wrong.

1180
01:17:35,955 --> 01:17:38,747
We are not your enemies, Banner.

1181
01:17:38,750 --> 01:17:39,823
Try to think!

1182
01:17:50,053 --> 01:17:51,857
Okay, the relays are intact.

1183
01:17:52,055 --> 01:17:53,300
What's our next move?

1184
01:17:53,598 --> 01:17:54,671
Even if I clear the rotors,

1185
01:17:54,724 --> 01:17:56,958
this thing won't
re-engage without a jump.

1186
01:17:57,101 --> 01:17:58,304
I'm going to have to
get in there and push.

1187
01:17:58,603 --> 01:18:00,236
If that thing gets up to
speed, you'll get shredded.

1188
01:18:00,480 --> 01:18:02,584
That stator control unit
can reverse the polarity

1189
01:18:02,607 --> 01:18:03,981
long enough to disengage
Maglev and that could...

1190
01:18:04,108 --> 01:18:05,311
Speak English!

1191
01:18:06,652 --> 01:18:07,855
You see that red lever?

1192
01:18:09,238 --> 01:18:11,258
It will slow the rotors down
long enough for me to get out.

1193
01:18:11,449 --> 01:18:13,167
Stand by it. Wait for my word.

1194
01:19:05,878 --> 01:19:07,468
We need full evac
on the lower hangar bay.

1195
01:19:10,883 --> 01:19:12,001
Grenade!

1196
01:19:27,024 --> 01:19:28,486
We've got a perimeter breach!

1197
01:19:28,526 --> 01:19:30,674
Hostiles are in S. H. I.E.L.D. gear.

1198
01:19:30,695 --> 01:19:32,886
Call-outs at every junction.

1199
01:19:40,037 --> 01:19:42,358
We have the Hulk and Thor
on Research Level 4.

1200
01:19:42,373 --> 01:19:43,920
Levels 2 and 3 are dark.

1201
01:19:44,083 --> 01:19:46,102
Sir, the Hulk will tear this place apart!

1202
01:19:47,170 --> 01:19:48,243
Get his attention.

1203
01:19:48,546 --> 01:19:52,841
Escort 6-0, proceed to
Wishbone and engage hostile.

1204
01:19:52,842 --> 01:19:54,217
Don't get too close.

1205
01:19:54,260 --> 01:19:55,420
COPY-

1206
01:20:07,565 --> 01:20:08,897
Target acquired.

1207
01:20:13,154 --> 01:20:14,155
Target engaged.

1208
01:20:25,666 --> 01:20:27,299
Target angry, target angry!

1209
01:21:35,820 --> 01:21:37,968
They're not getting through
here, so what the hell...

1210
01:21:56,424 --> 01:21:58,787
Engine one is now in shut-down.

1211
01:22:07,101 --> 01:22:09,378
We are in an uncontrolled descent.

1212
01:22:09,395 --> 01:22:11,156
Sir, we've lost all power in engine one.

1213
01:22:11,814 --> 01:22:13,747
It's Barton. He took out our systems.

1214
01:22:13,774 --> 01:22:16,352
He's headed for the detention level.

1215
01:22:16,360 --> 01:22:18,422
Does anybody copy?

1216
01:22:19,530 --> 01:22:21,764
This is Agent Romanoff.

1217
01:22:21,782 --> 01:22:23,329
I copy.

1218
01:22:27,580 --> 01:22:28,697
Stark, we 're losing altitude.

1219
01:22:28,998 --> 01:22:30,287
Yeah, I noticed.

1220
01:22:59,362 --> 01:23:00,393
No!

1221
01:23:08,120 --> 01:23:10,612
Are you ever not going to fall for that?

1222
01:23:53,791 --> 01:23:56,197
The humans think us immortal.

1223
01:23:57,169 --> 01:23:58,802
Should we test that?

1224
01:24:01,382 --> 01:24:02,499
Move away, please.

1225
01:24:07,138 --> 01:24:08,512
You like this?

1226
01:24:09,640 --> 01:24:12,733
We started working on the prototype
after you sent the Destroyer.

1227
01:24:14,103 --> 01:24:16,208
Even I don't know what it does.

1228
01:24:17,148 --> 01:24:18,480
Do you want to find out?

1229
01:24:20,401 --> 01:24:21,690
No!

1230
01:25:31,388 --> 01:25:32,892
Natasha?

1231
01:26:04,380 --> 01:26:06,227
You're going to lose.

1232
01:26:08,175 --> 01:26:09,293
Am I'.>

1233
01:26:10,678 --> 01:26:13,298
It's in your nature.

1234
01:26:15,349 --> 01:26:17,797
Your heroes are scattered.

1235
01:26:17,810 --> 01:26:21,646
Your floating fortress falls from the sky.

1236
01:26:21,647 --> 01:26:22,979
Where is my disadvantage?

1237
01:26:23,941 --> 01:26:25,831
You lack conviction.

1238
01:26:26,735 --> 01:26:27,809
I don't think I'm...

1239
01:26:34,702 --> 01:26:36,335
So, that's what it does.

1240
01:26:38,455 --> 01:26:40,174
All hands
to crash stations immediately.

1241
01:27:08,944 --> 01:27:09,975
Cap, hit the lever.

1242
01:27:10,613 --> 01:27:13,018
I need a minute here!

1243
01:27:13,282 --> 01:27:14,442
Lever

1244
01:27:14,491 --> 01:27:15,522
now!

1245
01:27:27,630 --> 01:27:28,832
Help!

1246
01:28:04,375 --> 01:28:05,836
Sorry, boss.

1247
01:28:05,876 --> 01:28:07,465
The god rabbited.

1248
01:28:07,711 --> 01:28:09,258
Just stay awake.

1249
01:28:09,296 --> 01:28:10,800
Eyes on me.

1250
01:28:11,048 --> 01:28:12,465
No, I'm clocking out here.

1251
01:28:12,716 --> 01:28:13,919
Not an option.

1252
01:28:15,219 --> 01:28:17,281
It's okay, boss.

1253
01:28:19,098 --> 01:28:21,246
This was never gonna work

1254
01:28:21,266 --> 01:28:22,469
if they didn't have something

1255
01:28:23,894 --> 01:28:25,398
to...

1256
01:28:54,550 --> 01:28:56,483
Agent Coulson is down.

1257
01:28:57,761 --> 01:28:59,566
A medical team is on
its way to your location.

1258
01:28:59,596 --> 01:29:01,143
They're here.

1259
01:29:04,268 --> 01:29:05,986
They called it.

1260
01:29:22,161 --> 01:29:23,879
These were in Phil Coulson's jacket.

1261
01:29:27,166 --> 01:29:29,399
I guess he never did
get you to sign them.

1262
01:29:32,963 --> 01:29:34,724
We're dead in the air up here.

1263
01:29:34,757 --> 01:29:37,979
Our communications,
the location of the Cube,

1264
01:29:38,260 --> 01:29:40,494
Banner, Thor...

1265
01:29:41,889 --> 01:29:43,693
I got nothing for you.

1266
01:29:43,724 --> 01:29:46,731
I lost my one good eye.

1267
01:29:49,646 --> 01:29:52,697
Maybe I had that coming.

1268
01:29:56,904 --> 01:29:58,278
Yes,

1269
01:29:59,323 --> 01:30:02,846
we were going to build
an arsenal with the Tesseract.

1270
01:30:04,161 --> 01:30:06,138
I never put all my chips
on that number, though

1271
01:30:06,163 --> 01:30:09,385
because I was playing
something even riskier.

1272
01:30:13,170 --> 01:30:17,466
There was an idea, Stark knows this,

1273
01:30:19,176 --> 01:30:22,699
called the Avengers Initiative.

1274
01:30:23,764 --> 01:30:25,998
The idea was to bring together a group

1275
01:30:26,016 --> 01:30:28,680
of remarkable people

1276
01:30:29,353 --> 01:30:32,274
to see if they could become
something more.

1277
01:30:33,524 --> 01:30:37,648
To see if they could work together
when we needed them to,

1278
01:30:37,694 --> 01:30:41,088
to fight the battles that we never could.

1279
01:30:43,951 --> 01:30:49,020
Phil Coulson died
still believing in that idea.

1280
01:30:51,166 --> 01:30:52,927
In heroes.

1281
01:31:00,884 --> 01:31:02,560
Well,

1282
01:31:03,345 --> 01:31:06,137
it's an old-fashioned notion.

1283
01:31:26,285 --> 01:31:28,690
You fell out of the sky.

1284
01:31:42,843 --> 01:31:44,132
Did I hurt anybody?

1285
01:31:44,428 --> 01:31:47,597
There's nobody around here to get hurt.

1286
01:31:47,598 --> 01:31:51,034
You did scare the hell
out of some pigeons, though.

1287
01:31:51,768 --> 01:31:52,886
Lucky.

1288
01:31:52,936 --> 01:31:54,311
Or just good aim.

1289
01:31:54,688 --> 01:31:56,020
You were awake when you fell.

1290
01:31:58,317 --> 01:32:00,164
- You saw?
- The whole thing.

1291
01:32:00,277 --> 01:32:01,995
Right through the ceiling.

1292
01:32:02,279 --> 01:32:06,324
Big and green and buck-ass nude.

1293
01:32:06,325 --> 01:32:07,527
Here.

1294
01:32:08,827 --> 01:32:11,104
Didn't think those would
fit you until you shrunk down

1295
01:32:11,121 --> 01:32:13,699
to a regular-size feller.

1296
01:32:15,918 --> 01:32:17,292
Thank you.

1297
01:32:18,003 --> 01:32:19,206
Are you an alien?

1298
01:32:19,796 --> 01:32:21,042
What?

1299
01:32:21,298 --> 01:32:22,715
From outer space, an alien.

1300
01:32:23,217 --> 01:32:24,290
No.

1301
01:32:24,885 --> 01:32:27,892
Well, then, son, you've got a condition.

1302
01:32:38,607 --> 01:32:41,055
Clint. You're going to be all right.

1303
01:32:44,488 --> 01:32:46,722
You know that?

1304
01:32:47,449 --> 01:32:49,382
Is that what you know?

1305
01:32:51,787 --> 01:32:54,751
I've got no window.

1306
01:32:55,249 --> 01:32:56,710
I have to flush him out.

1307
01:32:57,709 --> 01:32:59,642
You got to level out.
It's going to take time.

1308
01:32:59,670 --> 01:33:01,131
You don't understand.

1309
01:33:03,173 --> 01:33:06,266
Have you ever had someone
take your brain and play?

1310
01:33:07,219 --> 01:33:11,601
Pull you out
and stuff something else in?

1311
01:33:14,559 --> 01:33:16,793
Do you know what it's like
to be unmade?

1312
01:33:18,522 --> 01:33:20,756
You know that I do.

1313
01:33:28,198 --> 01:33:29,272
Why am I back?

1314
01:33:30,659 --> 01:33:32,120
How did you get him out?

1315
01:33:32,160 --> 01:33:34,952
Cognitive recalibration.

1316
01:33:35,122 --> 01:33:37,742
I hit you really hard on the head.

1317
01:33:37,749 --> 01:33:38,909
Thanks.

1318
01:33:43,338 --> 01:33:44,927
Natasha...

1319
01:33:45,549 --> 01:33:46,709
How many agents did I...

1320
01:33:46,758 --> 01:33:48,348
Don't.

1321
01:33:48,552 --> 01:33:50,700
Don't do that to yourself, Clint.

1322
01:33:51,346 --> 01:33:53,151
This is Loki.

1323
01:33:53,432 --> 01:33:55,880
This is monsters and magic,

1324
01:33:55,892 --> 01:33:57,310
and nothing we were ever trained for.

1325
01:33:57,436 --> 01:33:59,025
Loki, did he get away?

1326
01:33:59,062 --> 01:34:00,093
Yeah.

1327
01:34:00,689 --> 01:34:02,837
I don't suppose you know where.

1328
01:34:03,066 --> 01:34:04,956
I didn't need to know.

1329
01:34:04,985 --> 01:34:06,790
I didn't ask.

1330
01:34:09,990 --> 01:34:12,310
He's going to
make his play soon, though.

1331
01:34:12,617 --> 01:34:13,691
Today.

1332
01:34:13,910 --> 01:34:15,071
We got to stop him.

1333
01:34:15,662 --> 01:34:17,037
Yeah? Who's "we"?

1334
01:34:17,205 --> 01:34:19,096
I don't know. Whoever's left.

1335
01:34:20,542 --> 01:34:21,959
Well,

1336
01:34:23,587 --> 01:34:25,821
if I put an arrow
through Loki's eye socket,

1337
01:34:25,881 --> 01:34:28,673
I would sleep better, I suppose.

1338
01:34:31,261 --> 01:34:32,808
Now you sound like you.

1339
01:34:33,430 --> 01:34:34,976
But you don't.

1340
01:34:37,100 --> 01:34:40,061
You're a spy, not a soldier.

1341
01:34:40,062 --> 01:34:44,959
Now you want to wade into a war. Why?

1342
01:34:46,568 --> 01:34:48,630
What did Loki do to you?

1343
01:34:49,279 --> 01:34:51,814
He didn't. I just...

1344
01:34:55,452 --> 01:34:57,041
Natasha.

1345
01:34:59,081 --> 01:35:01,185
I've been compromised.

1346
01:35:04,127 --> 01:35:06,104
I got red in my ledger.

1347
01:35:08,382 --> 01:35:10,573
I would like to wipe it out.

1348
01:35:26,483 --> 01:35:28,116
Was he married?

1349
01:35:28,151 --> 01:35:29,612
No.

1350
01:35:29,653 --> 01:35:34,078
There was a cellist, I think.

1351
01:35:35,492 --> 01:35:36,996
I'm sorry.

1352
01:35:37,619 --> 01:35:39,080
He seemed like a good man.

1353
01:35:40,539 --> 01:35:41,741
He was an idiot.

1354
01:35:41,790 --> 01:35:43,938
Why? For believing?

1355
01:35:44,167 --> 01:35:45,628
For taking on Loki alone.

1356
01:35:45,669 --> 01:35:47,474
He was doing his job.

1357
01:35:47,504 --> 01:35:49,910
He was out of his league.
He should have waited.

1358
01:35:49,923 --> 01:35:51,040
He should have...

1359
01:35:51,341 --> 01:35:52,888
Sometimes there isn't a way out, Tony.

1360
01:35:53,051 --> 01:35:55,328
Right, I've heard that before.

1361
01:35:55,345 --> 01:35:56,548
Is this the first time you lost a soldier?

1362
01:35:56,847 --> 01:35:58,522
We are not soldiers.

1363
01:36:03,186 --> 01:36:04,819
I'm not marching to Fury's fife.

1364
01:36:05,063 --> 01:36:06,309
Neither am I.

1365
01:36:06,356 --> 01:36:08,676
He's got the same blood
on his hands that Loki does.

1366
01:36:08,692 --> 01:36:10,153
But right now,
we got to put that behind us

1367
01:36:10,193 --> 01:36:12,255
and get this done.

1368
01:36:12,404 --> 01:36:13,435
Loki needs a power source.

1369
01:36:13,488 --> 01:36:14,489
If we can put together a list...

1370
01:36:14,531 --> 01:36:15,562
He made it personal.

1371
01:36:15,866 --> 01:36:16,897
That's not the point.

1372
01:36:17,033 --> 01:36:19,526
That is the point. That's Loki's point.

1373
01:36:19,661 --> 01:36:21,379
He hit us all right where we live. Why?

1374
01:36:21,705 --> 01:36:22,778
To tear us apart.

1375
01:36:23,206 --> 01:36:24,753
Yeah, divide and conquer is great

1376
01:36:24,791 --> 01:36:27,369
but he knows he has to
take us out to win, right?

1377
01:36:27,377 --> 01:36:29,010
That's what he wants.

1378
01:36:29,045 --> 01:36:31,366
He wants to beat us,
he wants to be seen doing it.

1379
01:36:31,465 --> 01:36:32,582
He wants an audience.

1380
01:36:33,550 --> 01:36:35,268
Right. I caught his act in Stuttgart.

1381
01:36:35,302 --> 01:36:38,387
Yeah, that was just previews.
This is opening night.

1382
01:36:38,388 --> 01:36:41,052
And Loki, he's a full-tilt diva, right?

1383
01:36:41,057 --> 01:36:42,690
He wants flowers, he wants parades.

1384
01:36:42,726 --> 01:36:46,334
He wants a monument built to the skies
with his name plastered...

1385
01:36:48,273 --> 01:36:49,605
Son of a bitch.

1386
01:37:00,410 --> 01:37:01,570
Time to go.

1387
01:37:01,995 --> 01:37:03,542
- Go where?
- I'll tell you on the way.

1388
01:37:03,747 --> 01:37:04,748
Can you fly one of those jets?

1389
01:37:06,541 --> 01:37:07,572
I can.

1390
01:37:11,296 --> 01:37:12,456
You got a suit?

1391
01:37:12,631 --> 01:37:13,662
Yeah.

1392
01:37:13,924 --> 01:37:15,213
Then suit up.

1393
01:37:42,786 --> 01:37:44,203
Hey, you guys aren't
authorised to be in here.

1394
01:37:44,287 --> 01:37:46,521
Son, just don't.

1395
01:37:48,959 --> 01:37:49,960
Sir.

1396
01:37:50,001 --> 01:37:51,032
Agent Hill.

1397
01:37:51,753 --> 01:37:53,386
Those cards,

1398
01:37:55,465 --> 01:37:59,589
they were in Coulson's locker,
not in his jacket.

1399
01:38:03,974 --> 01:38:05,649
They needed the push.

1400
01:38:08,979 --> 01:38:11,212
We have an unauthorised departure
from Bay 6.

1401
01:38:11,898 --> 01:38:13,316
They found him.

1402
01:38:14,317 --> 01:38:18,153
Get our communications back up,
whatever you have to do.

1403
01:38:18,154 --> 01:38:20,346
- I want eyes on everything.
- Yes, sir.

1404
01:38:34,004 --> 01:38:35,808
Sir, I've turned off the arc reactor

1405
01:38:35,839 --> 01:38:39,800
but the device
is already self-sustaining.

1406
01:38:39,801 --> 01:38:42,078
Shut it down, Dr Selvig.

1407
01:38:42,304 --> 01:38:43,636
It's too late!

1408
01:38:45,724 --> 01:38:47,270
She can't stop now.

1409
01:38:48,518 --> 01:38:50,667
She wants to show us something!

1410
01:38:50,854 --> 01:38:53,045
A new universe.

1411
01:38:53,231 --> 01:38:54,434
Okay.

1412
01:39:01,823 --> 01:39:03,842
The barrier is pure energy.

1413
01:39:03,867 --> 01:39:05,542
It's unbreachable.

1414
01:39:05,827 --> 01:39:07,717
Yeah, I got that.

1415
01:39:08,538 --> 01:39:09,612
Plan B.

1416
01:39:10,999 --> 01:39:13,190
Sir, the Mark 7
is not ready for deployment.

1417
01:39:13,209 --> 01:39:15,358
Then skip the spinning rims.
We're on the clock.

1418
01:39:35,231 --> 01:39:38,023
Please tell me you're going
to appeal to my humanity.

1419
01:39:39,235 --> 01:39:41,598
Actually, I'm planning to threaten you.

1420
01:39:41,696 --> 01:39:43,200
You should have left
your Armour on for that.

1421
01:39:43,448 --> 01:39:44,952
Yeah.

1422
01:39:44,991 --> 01:39:46,194
It's seen a bit of mileage,

1423
01:39:46,242 --> 01:39:48,519
and you've got
the glow stick of destiny.

1424
01:39:49,621 --> 01:39:51,812
Would you like a drink?

1425
01:39:51,831 --> 01:39:53,077
Stalling me won't change anything.

1426
01:39:53,291 --> 01:39:55,568
No, no. Threatening.

1427
01:39:55,585 --> 01:39:56,703
No drink? Are you sure?

1428
01:39:57,087 --> 01:39:58,676
I'm having one.

1429
01:39:59,631 --> 01:40:03,712
The Chitauri are coming.
Nothing will change that.

1430
01:40:04,427 --> 01:40:05,587
What have I to fear?

1431
01:40:05,970 --> 01:40:07,474
The Avengers.

1432
01:40:09,766 --> 01:40:12,214
That's what we call ourselves.
We're sort of like a team.

1433
01:40:12,227 --> 01:40:13,945
"Earth's mightiest heroes"-type thing.

1434
01:40:13,978 --> 01:40:15,611
Yes, I've met them.

1435
01:40:15,772 --> 01:40:16,889
Yeah.

1436
01:40:17,148 --> 01:40:18,394
It takes us a while to get any traction,

1437
01:40:18,441 --> 01:40:19,559
I'll give you that one.

1438
01:40:19,609 --> 01:40:21,886
But let's do a head count, here.

1439
01:40:21,903 --> 01:40:24,523
Your brother, the demigod,

1440
01:40:26,116 --> 01:40:29,639
a super soldier, a living legend
who kind of lives up to the legend.

1441
01:40:29,828 --> 01:40:33,122
A man with breathtaking
anger-management issues,

1442
01:40:33,123 --> 01:40:36,130
a couple of master assassins,
and you, big fella,

1443
01:40:36,835 --> 01:40:39,584
you've managed to piss off
every single one of them.

1444
01:40:39,587 --> 01:40:40,661
That was the plan.

1445
01:40:41,047 --> 01:40:43,152
Not a great plan.

1446
01:40:43,174 --> 01:40:45,323
When they come,

1447
01:40:45,343 --> 01:40:46,890
and they will,

1448
01:40:46,928 --> 01:40:48,088
they'll come for you.

1449
01:40:48,138 --> 01:40:49,211
I have an army.

1450
01:40:49,264 --> 01:40:50,381
We have a Hulk.

1451
01:40:51,099 --> 01:40:52,560
I thought the beast had wandered off.

1452
01:40:52,600 --> 01:40:54,620
You're missing the point.
There is no throne.

1453
01:40:54,644 --> 01:40:58,554
There is no version of this
where you come out on top.

1454
01:40:58,815 --> 01:41:00,834
Maybe your army comes
and maybe it's too much for us,

1455
01:41:00,984 --> 01:41:03,046
but it's all on you.

1456
01:41:04,028 --> 01:41:05,189
Because if we can't protect the Earth,

1457
01:41:05,280 --> 01:41:08,330
you can be damn well sure
we'll avenge it.

1458
01:41:10,493 --> 01:41:13,620
How will your friends have time for me

1459
01:41:13,621 --> 01:41:15,254
when they are so busy fighting you?

1460
01:41:22,630 --> 01:41:23,704
This usually works.

1461
01:41:23,798 --> 01:41:26,719
Well, performance issues,
it's not uncommon.

1462
01:41:26,968 --> 01:41:28,686
One out of five...

1463
01:41:30,346 --> 01:41:33,439
Jarvis, anytime now.

1464
01:41:35,018 --> 01:41:37,896
You will all fall before me.

1465
01:41:37,896 --> 01:41:39,185
Deploy!

1466
01:41:39,397 --> 01:41:40,557
Deploy!

1467
01:42:08,051 --> 01:42:11,144
And there's one other
person you pissed off.

1468
01:42:11,888 --> 01:42:13,263
His name was Phil.

1469
01:42:37,121 --> 01:42:38,711
Right.

1470
01:42:38,748 --> 01:42:39,779
Army.

1471
01:43:52,363 --> 01:43:53,781
Loki!

1472
01:43:53,823 --> 01:43:55,628
Turn off the Tesseract, or I'll destroy it.

1473
01:43:55,658 --> 01:43:56,818
You can't.

1474
01:43:56,910 --> 01:43:58,886
There is no stopping it.

1475
01:43:59,120 --> 01:44:00,709
There is only

1476
01:44:00,830 --> 01:44:02,033
the war.

1477
01:44:02,165 --> 01:44:03,325
So be it.

1478
01:44:25,188 --> 01:44:26,993
Stark, we're on your three,
headed northeast.

1479
01:44:27,190 --> 01:44:29,252
What? Did you stop for drive-through?

1480
01:44:29,275 --> 01:44:31,080
Swing up Park. I'm going
to lay them out for you.

1481
01:44:49,420 --> 01:44:50,838
Sir, we have more incoming.

1482
01:44:50,880 --> 01:44:52,427
Fine. Let's keep them occupied.

1483
01:44:59,514 --> 01:45:01,103
- Nat?
- I see him.

1484
01:45:45,768 --> 01:45:48,045
We got to get back up there.

1485
01:46:39,322 --> 01:46:40,783
Stark, are you seeing this?

1486
01:46:41,699 --> 01:46:43,933
Seeing. Still working on believing.

1487
01:46:44,160 --> 01:46:45,577
Where's Banner?
Has he shown up yet?

1488
01:46:45,661 --> 01:46:46,779
Banner?

1489
01:46:46,829 --> 01:46:47,860
Just keep me posted.

1490
01:46:48,372 --> 01:46:50,649
Jarvis, find me a soft spot.

1491
01:46:53,169 --> 01:46:54,802
Look at this!

1492
01:46:54,837 --> 01:46:55,868
Look around you!

1493
01:46:57,173 --> 01:47:00,781
You think this madness
will end with your rule?

1494
01:47:01,177 --> 01:47:02,723
It's too late.

1495
01:47:04,180 --> 01:47:05,469
It's too late to stop it.

1496
01:47:05,515 --> 01:47:09,166
No. We can, together.

1497
01:47:16,025 --> 01:47:17,830
Sentiment.

1498
01:47:46,013 --> 01:47:48,334
We've got civilians
still trapped up here.

1499
01:47:49,267 --> 01:47:50,298
Loki.

1500
01:48:01,863 --> 01:48:03,710
They're fish in a barrel down there.

1501
01:48:09,287 --> 01:48:11,349
We got this. It's good. Go.

1502
01:48:11,372 --> 01:48:12,618
Do you think you can hold them off?

1503
01:48:12,665 --> 01:48:13,739
Captain,

1504
01:48:15,877 --> 01:48:18,626
it would be my genuine pleasure.

1505
01:48:45,573 --> 01:48:47,077
Just like Budapest all over again.

1506
01:48:47,909 --> 01:48:50,185
You and I remember Budapest
very differently.

1507
01:49:06,594 --> 01:49:07,625
It's going to be an hour

1508
01:49:07,678 --> 01:49:09,096
before they can
scramble the National Guard.

1509
01:49:09,138 --> 01:49:11,028
National Guard?

1510
01:49:11,849 --> 01:49:13,224
Does the army know
what's happening here?

1511
01:49:13,267 --> 01:49:14,298
Do we?

1512
01:49:15,811 --> 01:49:17,101
You need men in these buildings.

1513
01:49:17,146 --> 01:49:18,735
There are people inside and
they're going to be running

1514
01:49:18,773 --> 01:49:20,062
right into the line of fire.

1515
01:49:20,149 --> 01:49:22,126
You take them to the basements
or through the subway.

1516
01:49:22,151 --> 01:49:23,827
You keep them off the streets.

1517
01:49:23,861 --> 01:49:26,224
I need a perimeter as far back as 39th.

1518
01:49:26,614 --> 01:49:28,031
Why the hell
should I take orders from you?

1519
01:49:42,338 --> 01:49:43,583
I need men in those buildings.

1520
01:49:43,631 --> 01:49:45,822
Lead the people down
and away from the streets.

1521
01:49:45,841 --> 01:49:48,247
We're going to set up a perimeter
all the way down to 39th Street.

1522
01:49:58,813 --> 01:50:00,230
Well, we got its attention.

1523
01:50:00,523 --> 01:50:02,499
What the hell was step two?

1524
01:50:31,929 --> 01:50:33,003
What's the story upstairs?

1525
01:50:33,055 --> 01:50:35,075
The power surrounding the Cube
is impenetrable.

1526
01:50:35,099 --> 01:50:37,848
Thor's right. We got
to deal with these guys.

1527
01:50:37,852 --> 01:50:39,570
- How do we do this?
- As a team.

1528
01:50:39,603 --> 01:50:40,764
I have unfinished business with Loki.

1529
01:50:41,147 --> 01:50:42,220
Yeah? Well, get in line.

1530
01:50:42,273 --> 01:50:43,304
Save it.

1531
01:50:43,691 --> 01:50:45,195
Loki's going to keep
this fight focused on us,

1532
01:50:45,234 --> 01:50:46,308
and that's what we need.

1533
01:50:46,360 --> 01:50:48,121
Without him,
these things could run wild.

1534
01:50:48,154 --> 01:50:50,818
We got Stark up top.
He's going to need us to...

1535
01:50:58,456 --> 01:51:02,151
So, this all seems horrible.

1536
01:51:02,543 --> 01:51:03,703
I've seen worse.

1537
01:51:04,086 --> 01:51:05,204
Sorry.

1538
01:51:05,379 --> 01:51:07,957
No, we could use a little worse.

1539
01:51:08,299 --> 01:51:10,490
- Stark, we got him.
- Banner?

1540
01:51:10,634 --> 01:51:11,966
Just like you said.

1541
01:51:12,261 --> 01:51:14,925
Then tell him to suit up.
I'm bringing the party to you.

1542
01:51:21,437 --> 01:51:23,242
I don't see how that's a party.

1543
01:51:31,072 --> 01:51:32,103
Dr Banner.

1544
01:51:33,908 --> 01:51:35,998
Now might be a really good
time for you to get angry.

1545
01:51:36,577 --> 01:51:39,197
That's my secret, Captain.

1546
01:51:40,790 --> 01:51:42,164
I'm always angry-

1547
01:51:53,803 --> 01:51:55,264
Hold on!

1548
01:52:25,334 --> 01:52:26,751
Send the rest.

1549
01:52:33,467 --> 01:52:34,799
Guys.

1550
01:52:35,010 --> 01:52:36,300
Call it, Captain.

1551
01:52:36,345 --> 01:52:37,634
All right, listen up.

1552
01:52:37,680 --> 01:52:40,257
Until we can close that portal,
our priority is containment.

1553
01:52:40,458 --> 01:52:41,875
Barton, I want you on that roof.

1554
01:52:41,917 --> 01:52:43,894
Eyes on everything.
Call out patterns and strays.

1555
01:52:43,919 --> 01:52:45,137
Stark, you got the perimeter.

1556
01:52:45,187 --> 01:52:46,577
Anything gets
more than three blocks out,

1557
01:52:46,664 --> 01:52:48,239
you turn it back or you turn it to ash.

1558
01:52:48,324 --> 01:52:49,698
- Can you give me a lift?
- Right.

1559
01:52:49,750 --> 01:52:50,910
Better clench up, Legolas.

1560
01:52:54,530 --> 01:52:56,592
Thor, you got to try
and bottleneck that portal.

1561
01:52:56,866 --> 01:52:58,026
Slow them down.

1562
01:52:58,284 --> 01:53:00,217
You got the lightning.
Light the bastards up.

1563
01:53:02,546 --> 01:53:04,078
You and me,
we stay here on the ground.

1564
01:53:04,123 --> 01:53:05,326
We keep the fighting here.

1565
01:53:05,374 --> 01:53:06,405
And Hulk...

1566
01:53:09,044 --> 01:53:10,205
Smash.

1567
01:54:04,099 --> 01:54:05,260
Sir.

1568
01:54:05,976 --> 01:54:07,007
The Council is on.

1569
01:54:12,107 --> 01:54:15,243
Stark, you got a lot of strays
sniffing your tail.

1570
01:54:17,196 --> 01:54:19,129
I'm just trying to keep them
off the streets.

1571
01:54:19,365 --> 01:54:21,384
Well, they can't bank worth a damn.

1572
01:54:21,408 --> 01:54:22,654
So find a tight corner.

1573
01:54:22,826 --> 01:54:24,288
I will roger that.

1574
01:54:47,101 --> 01:54:48,346
Oh, boy.

1575
01:54:55,526 --> 01:54:57,244
Nice call.

1576
01:54:57,278 --> 01:54:58,567
What else you got?

1577
01:54:58,612 --> 01:55:01,531
Thor is taking on
a squadron down on Sixth.

1578
01:55:01,532 --> 01:55:03,551
And he didn't invite me.

1579
01:55:43,040 --> 01:55:45,102
Captain, none of this
is going to mean a damn thing

1580
01:55:45,126 --> 01:55:46,414
if we don't close that portal.

1581
01:55:46,468 --> 01:55:47,958
Our biggest guns couldn't touch it.

1582
01:55:47,995 --> 01:55:50,358
Well, maybe it's not about guns.

1583
01:55:52,133 --> 01:55:54,437
If you want to get up there,
you're going to need a ride.

1584
01:55:55,127 --> 01:55:56,287
I got a ride.

1585
01:55:57,338 --> 01:55:58,611
I could use a boost, though.

1586
01:56:01,050 --> 01:56:02,081
Are you sure about this?

1587
01:56:02,718 --> 01:56:05,124
Yeah. It's gonna be fun.

1588
01:56:32,247 --> 01:56:34,095
Okay, turn, turn.

1589
01:56:34,249 --> 01:56:36,097
Less!Less!

1590
01:57:58,667 --> 01:58:01,753
Captain, the bank
on 42nd past Madison.

1591
01:58:01,754 --> 01:58:03,644
They've cornered
a lot of civilians in there.

1592
01:58:03,672 --> 01:58:05,477
I'm on it.

1593
01:58:25,694 --> 01:58:27,412
Everyone! Clear out!

1594
01:58:57,392 --> 01:58:59,153
Director Fury,

1595
01:58:59,186 --> 01:59:00,775
the Council has made a decision.

1596
01:59:01,063 --> 01:59:03,941
I recognise the Council
has made a decision.

1597
01:59:03,941 --> 01:59:05,659
But given that
it's a stupid-ass decision,

1598
01:59:05,692 --> 01:59:07,196
I have elected to ignore it.

1599
01:59:07,236 --> 01:59:10,404
Director, you're closer
than any of our subs.

1600
01:59:10,405 --> 01:59:11,479
You scramble that jet...

1601
01:59:11,573 --> 01:59:14,452
That is the island of Manhattan,
Councilman.

1602
01:59:14,618 --> 01:59:16,852
Until I'm certain my team can't hold it,

1603
01:59:16,870 --> 01:59:18,932
I will not order a nuclear strike

1604
01:59:18,956 --> 01:59:20,330
against a civilian population.

1605
01:59:20,541 --> 01:59:22,817
If we don't hold them here,
we lose everything.

1606
01:59:23,085 --> 01:59:25,921
If I send that bird out, we already have.

1607
01:59:29,591 --> 01:59:30,966
You.

1608
01:59:33,554 --> 01:59:34,799
Hawkeye!

1609
01:59:35,848 --> 01:59:36,879
Nat, what are you doing?

1610
01:59:37,808 --> 01:59:38,839
A little help?

1611
01:59:44,231 --> 01:59:45,262
I got him.

1612
02:00:11,675 --> 02:00:12,706
Enough!

1613
02:00:13,302 --> 02:00:15,578
You are, all of you, beneath me!

1614
02:00:15,846 --> 02:00:18,764
I am a god, you dull creature.

1615
02:00:18,765 --> 02:00:20,355
And I will not be bullied by...

1616
02:00:29,818 --> 02:00:31,795
Puny god.

1617
02:00:40,078 --> 02:00:41,668
The sceptre...

1618
02:00:42,706 --> 02:00:44,038
Doctor.

1619
02:00:45,834 --> 02:00:48,794
Loki's sceptre. The energy.

1620
02:00:48,795 --> 02:00:50,514
The Tesseract can't fight,

1621
02:00:50,547 --> 02:00:52,437
but you can't protect against yourself.

1622
02:00:52,549 --> 02:00:53,623
It's not your fault.

1623
02:00:53,675 --> 02:00:55,193
You didn't know what you were doing.

1624
02:00:58,180 --> 02:01:00,456
Actually, I think I did.

1625
02:01:00,474 --> 02:01:03,567
I built in a safety
to cut their power source.

1626
02:01:04,603 --> 02:01:06,149
Loki's sceptre.

1627
02:01:06,188 --> 02:01:08,894
It may be able to close the portal.

1628
02:01:10,859 --> 02:01:12,749
And I'm looking right at it.

1629
02:01:25,165 --> 02:01:28,774
Sir, we will lose power
before we penetrate that shell.

1630
02:01:35,467 --> 02:01:38,886
Jarvis, you ever hear the tale of Jonah?

1631
02:01:38,887 --> 02:01:41,121
I wouldn't consider him a role model.

1632
02:02:50,876 --> 02:02:52,766
Director Fury is no longer in command.

1633
02:02:52,794 --> 02:02:54,943
Override order 7-Alpha-1-1.

1634
02:02:54,963 --> 02:02:57,498
7-Alpha-1-1, confirmed.
We're go for takeoff.

1635
02:02:58,467 --> 02:03:00,529
Sir, we have a bird in motion!

1636
02:03:01,011 --> 02:03:02,858
Anyone on the deck,
we have a rogue bird.

1637
02:03:03,138 --> 02:03:04,513
We need to shut it down!

1638
02:03:04,556 --> 02:03:06,618
Repeat, takeoff is not authorised.

1639
02:03:37,339 --> 02:03:39,615
Stark, do you hear me?

1640
02:03:39,633 --> 02:03:41,652
You have a missile
headed straight for the city.

1641
02:03:42,302 --> 02:03:43,763
HOW long?

1642
02:03:43,804 --> 02:03:45,995
Three minutes, max.

1643
02:03:46,014 --> 02:03:47,518
The payload
will wipe out Midtown.

1644
02:03:47,724 --> 02:03:49,657
Jarvis, put everything we got
into the thrusters.

1645
02:03:49,893 --> 02:03:51,654
1 just did

1646
02:04:04,324 --> 02:04:05,741
Package is sent.

1647
02:04:05,909 --> 02:04:08,959
Detonation in
2 minutes, 30 seconds, mark.

1648
02:04:31,810 --> 02:04:34,302
Are you ready for another bout?

1649
02:04:34,688 --> 02:04:35,961
What, are you getting sleepy?

1650
02:04:41,486 --> 02:04:43,334
Right at the crown!

1651
02:04:49,244 --> 02:04:51,177
I can close it.

1652
02:04:51,204 --> 02:04:52,965
Can anybody copy?

1653
02:04:53,039 --> 02:04:54,285
I can shut the portal down.

1654
02:04:54,583 --> 02:04:56,402
- Do it!
- No, wait.

1655
02:04:56,426 --> 02:04:57,972
Stark, these things are still coming.

1656
02:04:58,019 --> 02:04:59,050
I got a nuke coming in.

1657
02:04:59,104 --> 02:05:01,037
It's gonna blow in less than a minute.

1658
02:05:10,849 --> 02:05:12,567
And I know just where to put it.

1659
02:05:19,900 --> 02:05:22,348
Stark, you know that's a one-way trip.

1660
02:05:22,360 --> 02:05:23,821
Save the rest for the turn, J.

1661
02:05:23,862 --> 02:05:28,115
Sir, shall I try Miss Potts?

1662
02:05:28,116 --> 02:05:29,921
Might as well.

1663
02:05:32,078 --> 02:05:34,570
The streets of New York City
have become a battleground.

1664
02:05:34,581 --> 02:05:37,029
The Army is here trying
to contain the violence

1665
02:05:37,167 --> 02:05:38,756
but clearly, it is outmatched.

1666
02:05:38,960 --> 02:05:41,366
And I have to say,
in all my years of reporting,

1667
02:05:41,379 --> 02:05:44,215
I have never seen anything like this.

1668
02:05:44,466 --> 02:05:46,040
We have limited information
on the team

1669
02:05:46,051 --> 02:05:49,746
but we do know that
billionaire Tony Stark's Iron Man...

1670
02:07:03,211 --> 02:07:05,101
Come on, Stark.

1671
02:07:11,428 --> 02:07:12,630
Close it.

1672
02:07:32,699 --> 02:07:33,730
Son of a gun.

1673
02:07:38,580 --> 02:07:40,298
He's not slowing down.

1674
02:07:58,266 --> 02:07:59,598
Is he breathing?

1675
02:08:27,629 --> 02:08:28,874
What the hell?

1676
02:08:31,758 --> 02:08:33,992
What just happened?

1677
02:08:34,177 --> 02:08:36,368
Please tell me nobody kissed me.

1678
02:08:40,558 --> 02:08:42,062
We won.

1679
02:08:44,562 --> 02:08:45,937
All right, yay!

1680
02:08:45,980 --> 02:08:48,085
Hurray. Good job, guys.

1681
02:08:48,108 --> 02:08:51,158
Let's just not come in tomorrow.
Let's just take a day.

1682
02:08:52,070 --> 02:08:53,531
Have you ever tried shawarma?

1683
02:08:54,155 --> 02:08:56,346
There's a shawarma joint
about two blocks from here.

1684
02:08:56,366 --> 02:08:58,171
I don't know what it is,
but I want to try it.

1685
02:08:58,660 --> 02:09:00,034
We're not finished yet.

1686
02:09:05,083 --> 02:09:07,059
And then shawarma after.

1687
02:09:28,857 --> 02:09:31,262
If it's all the same to you,

1688
02:09:34,404 --> 02:09:36,165
I'll have that drink now.

1689
02:09:43,997 --> 02:09:46,101
Despite the devastation
of what has been confirmed

1690
02:09:46,124 --> 02:09:47,971
as an extraterrestrial attack,

1691
02:09:48,001 --> 02:09:49,590
the extraordinary heroics

1692
02:09:49,669 --> 02:09:51,488
of the group known as the Avengers

1693
02:09:51,513 --> 02:09:53,346
has been to many a cause
not only for comfort,

1694
02:09:53,381 --> 02:09:54,412
but for celebration.

1695
02:09:54,507 --> 02:09:57,042
It's just really great knowing
they're out there.

1696
02:09:57,051 --> 02:09:58,984
That someone is watching over us.

1697
02:09:59,012 --> 02:10:00,301
I love you, Thor!

1698
02:10:00,346 --> 02:10:02,151
And then these guys were like...

1699
02:10:02,182 --> 02:10:03,456
And then the air goes...

1700
02:10:03,500 --> 02:10:05,161
And this green guy walks up
and he goes...

1701
02:10:05,201 --> 02:10:06,319
I don't know.

1702
02:10:06,369 --> 02:10:08,889
I don't exactly feel safer
with those things out there.

1703
02:10:08,897 --> 02:10:12,065
It just seems that there's
a lot they're not telling us.

1704
02:10:12,066 --> 02:10:15,418
Superheroes in New York?
Give me a break.

1705
02:10:15,612 --> 02:10:17,631
These so-called "heroes"

1706
02:10:17,655 --> 02:10:19,030
have to be held responsible

1707
02:10:19,073 --> 02:10:21,394
for the destruction done to this city.

1708
02:10:21,409 --> 02:10:23,600
This was their fight.
Where are they now?

1709
02:10:23,620 --> 02:10:26,580
Tough questions are being asked
about the Avengers themselves.

1710
02:10:26,581 --> 02:10:27,698
Their sudden appearance

1711
02:10:27,749 --> 02:10:29,210
and equally sudden disappearance...

1712
02:10:29,250 --> 02:10:32,171
What, this is all somehow their fault?

1713
02:10:34,088 --> 02:10:37,353
Captain America saved my life.

1714
02:10:39,385 --> 02:10:42,971
Wherever he is, and
wherever any of them are,

1715
02:10:42,972 --> 02:10:44,562
I would just. ..

1716
02:10:45,266 --> 02:10:47,672
I would want to say thank you.

1717
02:10:50,063 --> 02:10:51,652
Where are the Avengers?

1718
02:10:51,940 --> 02:10:54,173
I'm not currently
tracking their whereabouts.

1719
02:10:54,192 --> 02:10:56,468
I'd say they've earned
a leave of absence.

1720
02:10:56,486 --> 02:10:58,161
And the Tesseract?

1721
02:10:58,196 --> 02:11:00,344
The Tesseract is where it belongs.

1722
02:11:00,907 --> 02:11:03,355
Out of our reach.

1723
02:11:03,493 --> 02:11:04,954
That's not your call.

1724
02:11:04,994 --> 02:11:06,068
I didn't make it.

1725
02:11:06,162 --> 02:11:08,311
I just didn't argue with the god that did.

1726
02:11:08,540 --> 02:11:10,258
So, you let him take it

1727
02:11:10,458 --> 02:11:12,176
and the war criminal, Loki,

1728
02:11:12,210 --> 02:11:14,057
who should be
answering for his crime.

1729
02:11:14,087 --> 02:11:16,492
I think he Will be.

1730
02:11:30,144 --> 02:11:32,593
I don't think you understand
what you've started,

1731
02:11:32,897 --> 02:11:35,260
letting the Avengers
loose on this world.

1732
02:11:35,608 --> 02:11:36,682
They're dangerous.

1733
02:11:37,026 --> 02:11:40,635
They surely are,
and the whole world knows it.

1734
02:11:41,239 --> 02:11:43,645
Every world knows it.

1735
02:11:44,242 --> 02:11:46,261
Was that the point of all this?

1736
02:11:46,494 --> 02:11:48,083
A statement?

1737
02:11:50,915 --> 02:11:52,462
A promise.

1738
02:12:00,883 --> 02:12:02,516
Sir, how does it work now?

1739
02:12:03,761 --> 02:12:05,866
They've gone their separate ways.

1740
02:12:05,888 --> 02:12:08,939
Some, pretty extremely far.

1741
02:12:09,559 --> 02:12:11,621
If we get into a situation like this again,

1742
02:12:11,644 --> 02:12:13,019
what happens then?

1743
02:12:13,062 --> 02:12:14,136
They'll come back.

1744
02:12:15,773 --> 02:12:17,320
Are you really sure about that?

1745
02:12:17,358 --> 02:12:18,389
I am.

1746
02:12:20,236 --> 02:12:21,568
Why?

1747
02:12:22,530 --> 02:12:24,463
Because we'll need them to.

1748
02:15:16,287 --> 02:15:18,907
Humans.

1749
02:15:20,041 --> 02:15:24,595
They are not the cowering
wretches we were promised.

1750
02:15:25,379 --> 02:15:27,613
They stand.

1751
02:15:28,382 --> 02:15:33,752
They are unruly,
and therefore cannot be ruled.

1752
02:15:41,813 --> 02:15:44,815
To challenge them

1753
02:15:44,816 --> 02:15:48,295
is to court death.

